WEBVTT

1
00:01:36.375 --> 00:01:39.000
Oh, good morning, my sunshine.

2
00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:40.208
[kisses]

3
00:01:40.291 --> 00:01:42.583
[groaning]

4
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.708
[chuckles]

5
00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.916
A candle with no cake?
Is that what that is?

6
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.416
A cake made of light and human warmth.
A recipe from Mother Moon.

7
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:52.750
I helped her make it.

8
00:01:53.583 --> 00:01:55.916
[singing "Happy Birthday"]

9
00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:03.875
Cheers to Vicenza!

10
00:02:04.625 --> 00:02:06.208
Oh, happy birthday, sweetheart.

11
00:02:07.458 --> 00:02:08.583
Thank you, Mom.

12
00:02:08.666 --> 00:02:11.958
Eighteen translation movements
of the Earth.

13
00:02:12.041 --> 00:02:14.708
Eighteen years.
Now your daughter is an adult.

14
00:02:14.791 --> 00:02:17.041
Oh, my Goddess! What did you wish for?

15
00:02:17.125 --> 00:02:18.791
To know who my dad is, obviously.

16
00:02:19.958 --> 00:02:21.750
Oh, sweetie-pie…

17
00:02:21.833 --> 00:02:25.875
Even on your 18th birthday, you're making
that same old wish you always make?

18
00:02:25.958 --> 00:02:26.875
Yes!

19
00:02:26.958 --> 00:02:29.250
-Don't you think it's a big deal?
-Mm-mm.

20
00:02:29.333 --> 00:02:31.416
Don't you know
how important this is to me?

21
00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.250
Of course I do, sweetie-pie.

22
00:02:33.333 --> 00:02:37.375
And you still don't think it's a big deal,
that I want to know who my father is?

23
00:02:37.458 --> 00:02:39.458
No, no, no. Not even a little bit.

24
00:02:39.541 --> 00:02:41.833
[scoffs]
You think you're always right, don't you?

25
00:02:41.916 --> 00:02:43.250
But I am, darling!

26
00:02:43.333 --> 00:02:45.708
Come on, Mom.
You know I have the right to know.

27
00:02:45.791 --> 00:02:49.000
Trust me, it's not the right time.
The moon's not aligned with Jupiter.

28
00:02:49.083 --> 00:02:51.666
Gosh! You're the most
insensitive person, you know?

29
00:02:52.666 --> 00:02:55.750
Um, Mommy needs
to talk to you, sweetheart.

30
00:02:55.833 --> 00:02:57.083
I have nothing to say.

31
00:02:57.166 --> 00:02:59.250
Okay, you just listen.
I'll do the talking.

32
00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:01.041
-I had a dream…
-Oh, please!

33
00:03:01.125 --> 00:03:02.958
No, I won't make you hug any goats.

34
00:03:03.041 --> 00:03:05.208
Twelve goats, Mom!
You made me hug 12 goats!

35
00:03:05.291 --> 00:03:08.791
Yeah, 12 goats, whatever, it's not that.
Mommy dreamt with a letter.

36
00:03:08.875 --> 00:03:11.416
The letter "I" for a country.
So I thought…

37
00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.125
Iran? Iraq? Ireland? Italy?

38
00:03:14.208 --> 00:03:18.958
But I know, I can feel it. It's India.
You know I can feel this kind of stuff.

39
00:03:19.041 --> 00:03:21.458
Yeah, I know, Mom.
But couldn't it be, I don't know,

40
00:03:21.541 --> 00:03:24.208
uh, Israel? Iceland? Ivory Coast?

41
00:03:25.333 --> 00:03:27.333
Uh, no. It's India for sure.

42
00:03:27.416 --> 00:03:29.208
I can feel something is there.

43
00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:32.541
-Will you come with me?
-Is Dad there?

44
00:03:32.625 --> 00:03:33.458
No.

45
00:03:33.541 --> 00:03:35.250
Uh, then, no. Thank you.

46
00:03:35.833 --> 00:03:37.333
You know what, Mom?

47
00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:39.500
I think there's something
for you to learn in India,

48
00:03:39.583 --> 00:03:42.125
and it'll be good for us
to take a break from each other.

49
00:03:42.708 --> 00:03:46.750
Vicenza Shakti Pravananda Oxalá
Sarahara Zalala da Silva.

50
00:03:46.833 --> 00:03:50.166
Is this how you speak to your mother?
Or even worse, of India?

51
00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:53.458
'Cause Mommy already taught you
we have to respect India.

52
00:03:53.541 --> 00:03:56.416
India is a state of mind,
a quantum consciousness.

53
00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.750
-It's there, inside you. Inside me.
-Mm-hmm.

54
00:03:59.833 --> 00:04:02.250
-Inside all of us.
-[groans]

55
00:04:03.125 --> 00:04:04.833
-[door opens]
-Vicenza!

56
00:04:04.916 --> 00:04:06.125
[door closes]

57
00:04:06.208 --> 00:04:07.541
[indistinct chattering]

58
00:04:07.625 --> 00:04:10.000
-[man] Happy birthday, Vicenza.
-[man 2] Happy birthday.

59
00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:10.958
Thank you.

60
00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:14.875
-Happy birthday, Vicenza!
-Happy birthday!

61
00:04:14.958 --> 00:04:17.000
Thank you, girls! [chuckling]

62
00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:21.458
-[men and women] Happy birthday, Vicenza!
-In gratitude!

63
00:04:26.916 --> 00:04:28.875
-Happy birthday, Vicenza.
-In gratitude!

64
00:04:28.958 --> 00:04:30.916
Happy birthday, Vicenza!

65
00:04:32.083 --> 00:04:34.291
-Happy birthday, Vicenza.
-Oh…

66
00:04:34.833 --> 00:04:36.916
-Thank you.
-[man 3] Happy birthday, Vicenza.

67
00:04:40.333 --> 00:04:42.916
-[man and woman] Happy birthday, Vicenza!
-In gratitude.

68
00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.583
-Happy birthday, Vicenza.
-Thank you.

69
00:04:49.708 --> 00:04:50.916
Happy birthday, Vicenza!

70
00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.791
Aw, thank you!

71
00:05:47.291 --> 00:05:49.291
-I knew I would find you here!
-[gasps]

72
00:05:49.375 --> 00:05:51.125
[both laughing]

73
00:05:51.208 --> 00:05:53.375
Happy birthday, Vicenza!

74
00:05:53.458 --> 00:05:57.166
I wish you many moons! Millions of moons!

75
00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.458
[woman chuckling]

76
00:05:58.541 --> 00:06:00.041
I got you a little something.

77
00:06:00.125 --> 00:06:02.250
Thank you, Mother Moon!

78
00:06:02.333 --> 00:06:05.375
Look, I got you some aloe,
spinach, and taro too.

79
00:06:05.458 --> 00:06:08.916
You need to moisturize your hair.
It's not shining, my love.

80
00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.708
-It needs to shine.
-Yeah.

81
00:06:11.666 --> 00:06:13.208
[Mother Moon] Is that you?

82
00:06:13.291 --> 00:06:16.500
Yes. I'm trying to finish it,
but it's getting tough.

83
00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:21.291
You have to know yourself better
be able to make a self-portrait.

84
00:06:21.375 --> 00:06:22.666
You're right, Mother Moon.

85
00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:25.666
But how can I know myself better
if I don't even know my father?

86
00:06:27.291 --> 00:06:28.291
Can you talk to Mom?

87
00:06:28.875 --> 00:06:32.000
I've talked to her a thousand times.
But you know how Raion is.

88
00:06:32.083 --> 00:06:35.083
She won't listen to anyone
when it comes to this subject.

89
00:06:38.958 --> 00:06:39.791
[kisses]

90
00:06:41.166 --> 00:06:42.541
[thunder crashing]

91
00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.958
-Oh, Mom!
-My little sweetie-pie!

92
00:06:52.041 --> 00:06:53.083
[kisses]

93
00:06:53.166 --> 00:06:56.333
Oh, Mom. Safe travels.
Take care, okay?

94
00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:59.250
Of course. Oh, my love,
I'm gonna miss you so much!

95
00:06:59.333 --> 00:07:00.208
Me too.

96
00:07:00.291 --> 00:07:01.791
-[Mother Moon] Raion!
-[Raion] Hi!

97
00:07:01.875 --> 00:07:05.375
Oh, Mother Moon!
Get her safely to the airport, okay?

98
00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:08.791
Let's go, I'll take care of her.
But we're late, kid! Super behind!

99
00:07:08.875 --> 00:07:11.250
Hold on. Give me just a minute, please.

100
00:07:13.541 --> 00:07:17.000
Blessed be the Moroccan angels,
the shamanic healing,

101
00:07:17.083 --> 00:07:18.500
the odorless Erê.

102
00:07:18.583 --> 00:07:21.291
And bless the nature
that takes care of all of that.

103
00:07:21.375 --> 00:07:23.791
-Our whole orientation lies with it.
--Perfect.

104
00:07:23.875 --> 00:07:24.708
[chuckles]

105
00:07:24.791 --> 00:07:27.250
-Bless the lettuce sprout!
-[chuckling]

106
00:07:27.333 --> 00:07:29.416
-One more thing.
-Mm-hmm.

107
00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:33.333
If you feel the necessity
to do something insane, sweetheart,

108
00:07:33.416 --> 00:07:37.750
and listen well, I didn't say "desire,"
I said "necessity"--

109
00:07:37.833 --> 00:07:39.125
then listen to your heart.

110
00:07:39.208 --> 00:07:42.166
Because if your heart,
and only your heart,

111
00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:44.041
compels you to insanity…

112
00:07:45.125 --> 00:07:47.958
-Then go, hold tight to Ganesha and go.
-Okay!

113
00:07:49.041 --> 00:07:50.125
Oh, my love.

114
00:07:50.208 --> 00:07:51.041
[kisses]

115
00:07:51.125 --> 00:07:53.125
[engine revving]

116
00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:56.083
[Raion] I love you so much, sweetie!

117
00:07:57.666 --> 00:07:58.500
Bye!

118
00:08:01.833 --> 00:08:02.916
[exhales]

119
00:08:16.333 --> 00:08:17.375
[exhales]

120
00:08:28.625 --> 00:08:30.541
-[gasps]
-[frame clatters]

121
00:08:35.625 --> 00:08:38.500
RIO, CARNIVAL OF 2002
SANTA TERESA'S TROUPE, RAION AND PACO

122
00:08:48.291 --> 00:08:50.625
"Santa Teresa's Troupe. Raion and Paco."

123
00:08:53.583 --> 00:08:54.708
[exhales]

124
00:09:03.083 --> 00:09:04.125
[sighs]

125
00:09:09.333 --> 00:09:11.333
[bugs chittering]

126
00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:23.958
[chuckles softly]

127
00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:34.708
["Casa" by Nina Fernandes playing]

128
00:09:34.791 --> 00:09:36.916
COSMIC UNIVERSE

129
00:10:00.875 --> 00:10:02.583
FOR SALE

130
00:10:03.625 --> 00:10:04.916
[man] How much is it?

131
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.833
[gasps] Three hundred. Thank you.

132
00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:11.750
-A ticket to Rio de Janeiro, please.
-Okay.

133
00:10:58.291 --> 00:10:59.666
Go straight down that way.

134
00:11:35.291 --> 00:11:36.375
Hey, ma'am?

135
00:11:37.583 --> 00:11:39.875
Why are people throwing money at me?

136
00:11:39.958 --> 00:11:41.000
What?

137
00:11:41.083 --> 00:11:42.958
-Aren't you begging?
-No!

138
00:11:44.291 --> 00:11:45.958
Not that I don't need money…

139
00:11:46.458 --> 00:11:48.458
Do you know where Santa Teresa is?

140
00:11:58.875 --> 00:12:00.625
-In gratitude!
-Good luck!

141
00:12:00.708 --> 00:12:01.666
With all my heart.

142
00:12:16.458 --> 00:12:18.208
[boy] Amoeba party! Woo-hoo!

143
00:12:18.291 --> 00:12:20.750
-What's up? Check out the Naked Amoeba.
-The party!

144
00:12:20.833 --> 00:12:22.958
-[boy] In two weeks!
-[boy 2] We'll have music!

145
00:12:23.041 --> 00:12:24.958
Bring family, friends. You'll love it!

146
00:12:25.041 --> 00:12:28.250
Excuse me. Naked Amoeba's party.
It's in two weeks, okay?

147
00:12:28.333 --> 00:12:30.791
[boy 2] We're gonna have music.
I'll be playing too.

148
00:12:30.875 --> 00:12:34.125
Yeah, other people will play too.
Hey, guys, what's up?

149
00:12:34.208 --> 00:12:36.458
Naked Amoeba's party, okay?
It's in two weeks.

150
00:12:36.541 --> 00:12:39.208
-We're gonna have music.
-Naked Amoeba. In two weeks.

151
00:12:39.291 --> 00:12:40.500
[boy] It'll be like a rave.

152
00:12:40.583 --> 00:12:42.208
[boy 2] Yeah, we'll have live music!

153
00:12:42.291 --> 00:12:44.041
[boy] Naked Amoeba!

154
00:12:45.166 --> 00:12:47.875
-Check out the Amoeba Party!
-[girl] Check the party out!

155
00:12:47.958 --> 00:12:50.083
[girl 2] Whoa!
Pay attention to what you're doing!

156
00:12:50.166 --> 00:12:52.416
-[boy] Sorry.
-[girl 2] You almost dropped me.

157
00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:55.458
-I know. Sorry.
-[girl 2] Dude, pay attention.

158
00:12:55.541 --> 00:12:57.958
-Jesus, what are you looking at?
-Nothing, nothing.

159
00:13:08.958 --> 00:13:10.041
-Excuse me, hi.
-Hi.

160
00:13:10.125 --> 00:13:11.833
-Where this is address?
-It's here.

161
00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:13.833
-Thank you.
-Sure.

162
00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:30.500
PACO'S STUDIO

163
00:13:38.416 --> 00:13:39.333
[intercom buzzes]

164
00:13:43.041 --> 00:13:44.583
[exhales]

165
00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:52.166
Yes? What do you want
so early in the morning?

166
00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:54.083
[chuckles] It's 2:15 p.m.

167
00:13:54.708 --> 00:13:55.791
Good afternoon!

168
00:13:55.875 --> 00:13:57.708
Oh, boy. She's a hugger.

169
00:13:57.791 --> 00:14:00.208
Um… I'm, uh, looking for Paco.

170
00:14:00.291 --> 00:14:02.041
Oh, Paco. Is it about classes?

171
00:14:02.125 --> 00:14:04.291
-Yes! It's about classes!
-Great. Come on in.

172
00:14:04.375 --> 00:14:05.958
-Thank you.
-Sure.

173
00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:09.958
Hold on! Wait, not so fast. Hold on.

174
00:14:11.041 --> 00:14:11.916
Paco!

175
00:14:13.333 --> 00:14:14.333
Paco!

176
00:14:15.125 --> 00:14:16.125
Paco!

177
00:14:34.583 --> 00:14:36.416
What's with all the yelling, Josie?

178
00:14:36.958 --> 00:14:38.750
It's Jade. Ja-de.

179
00:14:38.833 --> 00:14:40.041
[Paco] Yeah, Jade.

180
00:14:40.125 --> 00:14:41.416
[refrigerator opens]

181
00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:44.750
Pssst. That girl wants to talk to you.

182
00:14:49.041 --> 00:14:50.708
-Who is she?
-I have no idea.

183
00:14:53.583 --> 00:14:55.041
[groans]

184
00:14:55.541 --> 00:14:57.500
-Hey, how are you?
-Hey, Paco.

185
00:14:58.458 --> 00:15:00.583
I'm here to discuss classes with you.

186
00:15:01.583 --> 00:15:03.041
But today's a Saturday.

187
00:15:03.958 --> 00:15:07.083
-It's Saturday.
-It's just, I came a long way to meet you.

188
00:15:07.791 --> 00:15:10.875
Listen, you come back on Monday,
and we'll talk, okay?

189
00:15:10.958 --> 00:15:13.833
Oh, Paco. I need your help for a second.
Could you come here?

190
00:15:13.916 --> 00:15:16.708
Just a second. Stay there.
He'll be right back, okay?

191
00:15:18.916 --> 00:15:22.916
Look, I don't mean to pry, but…
you haven't sold a painting in a while.

192
00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:26.333
These classes
have been helping you make ends meet.

193
00:15:26.416 --> 00:15:28.666
Let me tell you a secret,
I don't like teaching.

194
00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:31.333
I hate doing push-ups, but I do them.
That's life.

195
00:15:32.291 --> 00:15:33.666
[Paco sighs]

196
00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:35.083
Go over there. Talk to her.

197
00:15:35.166 --> 00:15:36.416
Go.

198
00:15:37.333 --> 00:15:38.208
Look at her.

199
00:15:44.208 --> 00:15:47.041
-You said you came a long way?
-Ten hours on the bus.

200
00:15:47.958 --> 00:15:49.708
I'll make an exception for you.

201
00:15:50.416 --> 00:15:53.041
Just give me a minute to, uh…
wash my face.

202
00:15:53.125 --> 00:15:54.291
Vicenza!

203
00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:56.791
My name is Vicenza.

204
00:15:56.875 --> 00:16:00.125
It's the mix of "Vicente" and "Zana,"
my maternal grandparents.

205
00:16:04.916 --> 00:16:05.958
[Paco scoffs]

206
00:16:10.166 --> 00:16:11.000
[chuckles]

207
00:16:19.458 --> 00:16:21.041
Don't touch that.

208
00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:23.416
Don't touch that, okay?

209
00:16:24.083 --> 00:16:26.333
Tell me, why do you want to have classes?

210
00:16:26.416 --> 00:16:30.083
It's because I'm having trouble
with my self-portrait.

211
00:16:30.166 --> 00:16:33.416
-I think I've got a creative block.
-Welcome to the club.

212
00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:35.708
I haven't painted anything in five years.

213
00:16:35.791 --> 00:16:37.041
-Really?
-Really.

214
00:16:37.625 --> 00:16:38.750
It happens, though.

215
00:16:39.333 --> 00:16:42.333
Let me tell you,
I'm not the most patient person.

216
00:16:42.416 --> 00:16:46.125
So to teach, I handpick my students,
the ones I think are worth it.

217
00:16:46.208 --> 00:16:47.708
Do you have anything to show me?

218
00:16:47.791 --> 00:16:49.541
No, but I can draw something quickly.

219
00:16:49.625 --> 00:16:51.541
-Don't worry about it.
-It's okay.

220
00:16:51.625 --> 00:16:53.333
No, look, you don't have to.

221
00:17:03.416 --> 00:17:04.250
Listen to me.

222
00:17:05.166 --> 00:17:07.083
You really don't have to, okay?

223
00:17:23.666 --> 00:17:25.375
-Is that me?
-Mm-hmm.

224
00:17:28.416 --> 00:17:30.916
Okay. So you can come back on Monday.

225
00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:33.500
Okay, let's go.
I'll walk you to the door. Come on.

226
00:17:34.125 --> 00:17:35.916
-Uh, Paco?
-Mm-hmm?

227
00:17:36.875 --> 00:17:37.833
I'm Raion's daughter.

228
00:17:42.666 --> 00:17:43.541
Raion?

229
00:17:44.875 --> 00:17:46.000
[chuckling]

230
00:17:46.083 --> 00:17:48.125
Your mom's Raion?

231
00:17:48.208 --> 00:17:50.000
Look at that!

232
00:17:51.875 --> 00:17:53.375
Do you remember this Carnival?

233
00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:57.583
[Paco] I do.

234
00:17:57.666 --> 00:17:59.500
Of course I remember. [chuckles]

235
00:18:00.125 --> 00:18:02.791
-You were 30 years old, right?
-Yeah.

236
00:18:02.875 --> 00:18:04.250
I think so, 30.

237
00:18:04.833 --> 00:18:06.208
And right now you're 48.

238
00:18:06.291 --> 00:18:09.666
Yes, but it doesn't show, right?
People usually think I'm 40, tops.

239
00:18:10.208 --> 00:18:11.416
Raion…

240
00:18:14.458 --> 00:18:15.666
It's gotta be the beard.

241
00:18:16.333 --> 00:18:17.791
People lie, Paco.

242
00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:25.000
What about Raion? Is she still living
in that community? The Namaste?

243
00:18:25.666 --> 00:18:27.458
Cosmic Universe. Mm-hmm.

244
00:18:27.541 --> 00:18:28.541
Mm.

245
00:18:29.375 --> 00:18:30.458
That's pretty sweet.

246
00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.583
I might be your daughter, Paco.

247
00:18:38.666 --> 00:18:40.083
[door opens]

248
00:18:40.166 --> 00:18:41.958
-[Jade] Paco.
-[door closes]

249
00:18:42.041 --> 00:18:45.041
Look, I can't wait for you, okay?
I'm out.

250
00:18:45.125 --> 00:18:46.458
Bye, little doll.

251
00:18:46.541 --> 00:18:48.208
-Bye.
-So cute. Bye.

252
00:18:48.833 --> 00:18:49.666
[kisses]

253
00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:52.208
Call me, okay?
You know what? I'll call you.

254
00:18:56.916 --> 00:18:58.916
[footsteps fade]

255
00:19:02.083 --> 00:19:04.875
So how long are you planning
to stand there speechless?

256
00:19:04.958 --> 00:19:08.458
I need to know if I should stay here,
or if I should get some water, tea…

257
00:19:08.541 --> 00:19:09.666
No, it's just, uh…

258
00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:12.583
[chuckling nervously]

259
00:19:14.791 --> 00:19:17.291
Raion never said anything.
She never reached out…

260
00:19:17.958 --> 00:19:18.791
Can I talk to her?

261
00:19:18.875 --> 00:19:21.250
She's in India, totally out of reach.

262
00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:24.750
[Paco hyperventilating]

263
00:19:26.916 --> 00:19:28.916
-I see.
-Can I get you anything?

264
00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:31.250
-Are you okay?
-A pillow.

265
00:19:31.333 --> 00:19:33.541
-Huh?
-A pillow. Just a pillow.

266
00:19:33.625 --> 00:19:35.791
-Okay.
-[Paco panting]

267
00:19:38.375 --> 00:19:43.041
[groaning]

268
00:19:43.125 --> 00:19:44.833
I'm going out. I'm going out.

269
00:19:44.916 --> 00:19:46.125
-Where to?
-I don't know.

270
00:19:46.208 --> 00:19:47.583
Can I go with you?

271
00:19:47.666 --> 00:19:50.416
-Where's your mother staying, again?
-I don't know.

272
00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.875
-What about you? Where are you staying?
-Nowhere.

273
00:19:52.958 --> 00:19:55.666
God, it gets worse.
Come, I'll take you to a place nearby.

274
00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:57.000
But wait! My bag, Paco!

275
00:19:57.083 --> 00:19:59.000
I got it, I got it.
Got it, got it, got it.

276
00:19:59.083 --> 00:20:01.083
I got it! There it is.

277
00:20:01.166 --> 00:20:02.500
-Now let's go!
-Calm down!

278
00:20:02.583 --> 00:20:03.458
Breathe.

279
00:20:04.583 --> 00:20:05.916
I just wanted to meet you.

280
00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:08.291
It's a pleasure. Shall we?

281
00:20:08.875 --> 00:20:09.750
Let's go.

282
00:20:09.833 --> 00:20:12.416
Go, go, go, go. Go, go, go.

283
00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:13.833
Go, go, go.

284
00:20:16.875 --> 00:20:18.625
-[Paco] Arthur!
-[Arthur] Hey!

285
00:20:18.708 --> 00:20:19.666
I'm here!

286
00:20:20.458 --> 00:20:22.333
-Hey, Arthur. Everything good?
-Mm!

287
00:20:22.416 --> 00:20:23.375
-Good.
-Good?

288
00:20:23.458 --> 00:20:25.125
-This is, uh…
-Vicenza.

289
00:20:25.208 --> 00:20:26.291
Vicenza, Arthur.

290
00:20:26.375 --> 00:20:27.750
-Arthur, Vicenza.
-How are you?

291
00:20:27.833 --> 00:20:30.000
Vicenza needs our help.
Do you have a room?

292
00:20:30.083 --> 00:20:33.291
Any room available?
I'll pay you later.

293
00:20:36.333 --> 00:20:38.375
[indistinct conversation continues]

294
00:20:40.208 --> 00:20:42.208
-[Paco] Vicenza? Vicenza.
-Mm?

295
00:20:42.291 --> 00:20:44.791
-Write my number down.
-I didn't bring my phone.

296
00:20:44.875 --> 00:20:47.250
-What?
-I don't use it much, I didn't bring it.

297
00:20:47.958 --> 00:20:51.125
She doesn't use her phone.
Uh, call me if you need me.

298
00:20:51.208 --> 00:20:54.166
Okay? Arthur knows where to find me.
So, bye-bye. Bye!

299
00:20:56.291 --> 00:20:59.916
[chuckles] Look, don't worry.
He's always like that.

300
00:21:00.625 --> 00:21:02.791
Welcome to our humble home.

301
00:21:02.875 --> 00:21:05.250
-Thank you.
-Come, I'll show you to your room.

302
00:21:23.166 --> 00:21:24.208
[intercom buzzes]

303
00:21:24.708 --> 00:21:25.666
[Paco] Coming!

304
00:21:29.208 --> 00:21:31.000
-What, it's Monday already?
-No.

305
00:21:31.083 --> 00:21:34.333
I came to see if you wanted me
to make you some breakfast.

306
00:21:34.416 --> 00:21:36.333
So we can learn a bit about each other.

307
00:21:47.750 --> 00:21:49.458
Here. You'll feel better.

308
00:21:49.541 --> 00:21:51.083
[groans]

309
00:21:52.958 --> 00:21:54.625
You're trying to kill me.

310
00:21:54.708 --> 00:21:56.333
Trust me. It's good for you.

311
00:21:56.416 --> 00:21:57.708
[groaning]

312
00:21:59.708 --> 00:22:01.416
-Mmm.
-[groaning]

313
00:22:02.041 --> 00:22:03.750
[gagging]

314
00:22:03.833 --> 00:22:06.458
This juice is good for headaches,
stomach aches, stress…

315
00:22:06.541 --> 00:22:09.083
Okay. If I drink it,
will you be nice and quiet?

316
00:22:09.166 --> 00:22:10.916
-Nice and quiet.
-Awesome.

317
00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:12.291
Oh.

318
00:22:12.375 --> 00:22:13.750
Before I forget…

319
00:22:14.541 --> 00:22:16.041
I dug around to find a phone.

320
00:22:16.625 --> 00:22:18.083
It's my old cell phone.

321
00:22:18.750 --> 00:22:20.166
-Okay?
-Mm-hmm.

322
00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:23.666
If you have to speak to me,
just give me a call. There you go.

323
00:22:24.875 --> 00:22:26.125
[groaning]

324
00:22:30.541 --> 00:22:32.500
-Do you know how to use it?
-Of course.

325
00:22:32.583 --> 00:22:34.250
But this one is better than mine.

326
00:22:34.833 --> 00:22:35.916
[groaning]

327
00:22:37.125 --> 00:22:38.333
[Paco muttering]

328
00:22:38.416 --> 00:22:41.291
Fine, I get it. You want to sleep,
so you want me to go.

329
00:22:41.375 --> 00:22:43.250
-Yes. Think you could?
-Mm-hmm.

330
00:22:43.333 --> 00:22:44.375
Fantastic.

331
00:22:44.458 --> 00:22:46.875
-In that case, we can talk later, okay?
-Sure.

332
00:22:46.958 --> 00:22:48.333
Ah, there you go.

333
00:22:51.708 --> 00:22:53.000
Mm! The juice!

334
00:22:54.958 --> 00:22:57.500
["Tão Bem" by Melim playing]

335
00:22:58.250 --> 00:22:59.416
[chuckles]

336
00:24:18.250 --> 00:24:19.458
You're welcome.

337
00:24:20.458 --> 00:24:21.416
"You're welcome"?

338
00:24:22.916 --> 00:24:24.333
You're welcome for what?

339
00:24:24.416 --> 00:24:27.125
Did I happen to say
you could go through my stuff?

340
00:24:28.125 --> 00:24:29.333
-Did I?
-[bucket clatters]

341
00:24:30.083 --> 00:24:31.083
Sorry, I…

342
00:24:31.166 --> 00:24:33.458
What did you do to my house, huh?
What's this?

343
00:24:33.541 --> 00:24:34.375
Look at my desk!

344
00:24:36.083 --> 00:24:38.708
-Weren't you leaving?
-Paco, I was just trying to help.

345
00:24:38.791 --> 00:24:40.125
Did I ask for your help?

346
00:24:40.208 --> 00:24:42.583
No, but I thought…

347
00:24:42.666 --> 00:24:45.708
I thought all of that mess
was blocking your inspiration.

348
00:24:45.791 --> 00:24:46.916
Blocking my inspiration?

349
00:24:47.000 --> 00:24:51.041
Now the energy will be able to flow.
The creativity will come back! You'll see!

350
00:24:51.125 --> 00:24:53.625
I'll show you how I get energy to flow.

351
00:24:54.541 --> 00:24:55.375
Go away!

352
00:24:59.166 --> 00:25:00.541
[papers rustle]

353
00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:09.875
Go away!

354
00:25:25.875 --> 00:25:28.083
-[boy singing]
-[music playing]

355
00:25:42.458 --> 00:25:45.666
We'll practice till day of the party.
Sounds good? Thanks, guys.

356
00:25:48.625 --> 00:25:50.833
-Hey!
-You weren't here earlier, right?

357
00:25:50.916 --> 00:25:53.208
I wasn't. So you're
the new guest, I'm assuming.

358
00:25:54.416 --> 00:25:56.250
Cool! [chuckling]

359
00:25:56.333 --> 00:25:59.125
-You're already dressed for the Carnival!
-No.

360
00:25:59.750 --> 00:26:01.708
No? I'm sorry.

361
00:26:01.791 --> 00:26:04.416
I'm not the best
when it comes to talking to girls.

362
00:26:04.500 --> 00:26:06.208
Especially when they're so pretty.

363
00:26:06.291 --> 00:26:07.666
-I mean, no.
-[chuckling]

364
00:26:07.750 --> 00:26:09.708
Yeah. Not that you're not pretty.

365
00:26:09.791 --> 00:26:12.083
-You're gorgeous, actually.
-[chuckles]

366
00:26:12.166 --> 00:26:15.041
I'm Arthur's grandson.
Arthur is my grandpa, you know?

367
00:26:15.125 --> 00:26:17.250
Of course, if I'm his grandson,
he's obviously…

368
00:26:17.333 --> 00:26:19.083
[chuckles] It's a pleasure. Cadu.

369
00:26:19.166 --> 00:26:20.041
Vicenza.

370
00:26:20.666 --> 00:26:23.083
How can I help you, Vicenza?
Do you need anything?

371
00:26:23.166 --> 00:26:25.916
Yo, Cadu. I found my instrument
for the troupe. The tuba.

372
00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:28.166
Cool, but I'm in the middle
of something here.

373
00:26:28.250 --> 00:26:30.083
You can listen too. Check this out.

374
00:26:31.458 --> 00:26:34.125
[tooting out of tune]

375
00:26:39.333 --> 00:26:41.625
It's just a little clogged,
but I'll fix it.

376
00:26:42.208 --> 00:26:43.333
So what do you think?

377
00:26:43.958 --> 00:26:47.041
-Why not start with something simpler?
-Why? You didn't like it?

378
00:26:47.125 --> 00:26:48.625
-I did!
-Really?

379
00:26:49.958 --> 00:26:51.500
Who's the weirdo in the costume?

380
00:26:52.041 --> 00:26:55.625
One, my name is Vicenza.
Two, this is not a costume.

381
00:26:56.208 --> 00:26:57.541
And three,

382
00:26:57.625 --> 00:26:59.875
you suck at playing the tuba.

383
00:26:59.958 --> 00:27:03.083
You're, like, the worst tuba player
I've ever heard.

384
00:27:03.166 --> 00:27:06.916
And I don't understand
why someone would tell you otherwise.

385
00:27:08.833 --> 00:27:10.000
[kisses]

386
00:27:10.083 --> 00:27:11.833
So Vicenza, I'm gonna go, okay?

387
00:27:11.916 --> 00:27:14.583
If you want to get my number
from Cadu, Prin-cenza…

388
00:27:14.666 --> 00:27:16.750
I could give you some tuba lessons and…

389
00:27:16.833 --> 00:27:17.958
[toots]

390
00:27:19.291 --> 00:27:20.416
Yeah.

391
00:27:20.500 --> 00:27:23.500
Cadu, give her my number, okay?
Thanks. Ah.

392
00:27:23.583 --> 00:27:26.583
Let me tell you something serious.
Cadu, pay attention.

393
00:27:26.666 --> 00:27:29.083
This thing you're doing,
always telling the truth…

394
00:27:29.166 --> 00:27:31.625
It's rare nowadays, right?
It's like a gift.

395
00:27:31.708 --> 00:27:33.791
When you have a gift,
share it with the world.

396
00:27:33.916 --> 00:27:36.291
If you don't,
you know what happens, don't you?

397
00:27:36.375 --> 00:27:38.041
-What?
-It bites you. Life's a snake!

398
00:27:38.125 --> 00:27:39.958
[hisses] Sorry.

399
00:27:40.041 --> 00:27:41.166
[kisses]

400
00:27:43.166 --> 00:27:45.958
Thanks. Big Nose, give me that drum
so I can make some noise!

401
00:27:46.041 --> 00:27:48.958
-"Life's a snake. Life makes you pay."
-[both chuckle]

402
00:27:49.041 --> 00:27:51.541
That's Nando, yeah. He's a character.

403
00:27:52.625 --> 00:27:54.583
You talked about me,
but you're quite handsome too.

404
00:27:54.666 --> 00:27:55.500
You think?

405
00:27:55.958 --> 00:27:57.958
[chuckling] Thank you.

406
00:27:58.458 --> 00:28:01.000
-I've never heard that from a girl before.
-You sure?

407
00:28:01.083 --> 00:28:02.000
I'm sure.

408
00:28:02.083 --> 00:28:05.125
I wish that was caught on camera
because nobody will believe me.

409
00:28:05.208 --> 00:28:06.833
Uh, hey weirdo.

410
00:28:06.916 --> 00:28:09.333
I see you trying
to get close to my brother,

411
00:28:09.416 --> 00:28:12.458
but everyone knows Paco's broke.
How's he paying for your stay?

412
00:28:12.541 --> 00:28:14.875
What's this, Betina?
Is this how you talk to people?

413
00:28:14.958 --> 00:28:17.916
She's right. I don't wanna stay here
at Paco's expense.

414
00:28:18.000 --> 00:28:20.833
But that doesn't justify your behavior.
Shall we try again?

415
00:28:21.583 --> 00:28:25.208
Betina, this is Vicenza.
Vicenza, this is my sister Betina.

416
00:28:25.291 --> 00:28:27.125
-Where's the money?
-She's the treasurer.

417
00:28:27.208 --> 00:28:28.666
-You can tell, right?
-Yeah.

418
00:28:28.750 --> 00:28:32.833
Look, I don't have money right now,
but I can find another way to pay.

419
00:28:32.916 --> 00:28:33.916
I could, um…

420
00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:35.916
I could teach yoga, for example.

421
00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:38.833
I could also fix things,
I could clean, or paint, cook…

422
00:28:38.916 --> 00:28:41.750
-Do you know how to sew?
-I'm a great seamstress.

423
00:28:41.833 --> 00:28:44.000
See? Wonderful! She can sew our sign!

424
00:28:44.083 --> 00:28:46.500
-Sure, and she can fix the sink too!
-Mm-hmm.

425
00:28:46.583 --> 00:28:49.291
No fixing the sink.
You know that's impossible, Betina.

426
00:28:50.208 --> 00:28:52.666
Nothing is impossible for Vicenza.

427
00:28:54.250 --> 00:28:56.166
-Show me the sink.
-[Betina chuckles]

428
00:29:29.333 --> 00:29:31.833
-Have you been living here long?
-Since my parents died.

429
00:29:31.916 --> 00:29:34.000
Oh, I'm so sorry.

430
00:29:34.083 --> 00:29:35.458
Don't worry. No problem.

431
00:29:36.583 --> 00:29:38.875
When I think about it,
ten years is a long time,

432
00:29:38.958 --> 00:29:40.625
living with my grandpa and my sister.

433
00:29:40.708 --> 00:29:41.625
And your grandma?

434
00:29:41.708 --> 00:29:42.958
My grandma…

435
00:29:43.583 --> 00:29:46.583
-I haven't seen her in five, six years.
-Oh, jeez.

436
00:29:46.666 --> 00:29:50.291
No, no. It's all good. Don't worry.
She left 'cause she wanted to.

437
00:29:50.791 --> 00:29:54.041
She left my grandpa tons of debt,
she stole…

438
00:29:54.125 --> 00:29:56.875
everything the troupe had.
He's never gotten over that.

439
00:29:56.958 --> 00:30:00.750
So that means he fills up the place
with guests and hosts classes

440
00:30:00.833 --> 00:30:04.750
as a way to pay his debts
and to keep his mind busy, right?

441
00:30:04.833 --> 00:30:08.791
Exactly. And that's why Betina and I
want to throw a party for the troupe.

442
00:30:08.875 --> 00:30:11.333
I don't know,
to try to cheer him up a little.

443
00:30:11.416 --> 00:30:14.958
I mean, I guess we're going for
a modern vibe or something.

444
00:30:15.041 --> 00:30:18.875
We don't want to just go with,
um, samba or Carnival songs.

445
00:30:18.958 --> 00:30:21.833
Betina thinks it's old-fashioned,
everyone does that.

446
00:30:21.916 --> 00:30:25.416
We want to try something new,
with a bit of an electronic vibe.

447
00:30:25.500 --> 00:30:27.958
-[groans]
-I know, I don't like the idea either.

448
00:30:28.041 --> 00:30:29.583
But I was outvoted, you know?

449
00:30:29.666 --> 00:30:31.875
We're even throwing a rave to raise money.

450
00:30:31.958 --> 00:30:34.375
-It's gonna be cool.
-What's up, Cadu?

451
00:30:34.458 --> 00:30:35.958
Lucinha! How are you doing?

452
00:30:36.041 --> 00:30:37.750
-Everything good?
-I missed you!

453
00:30:37.833 --> 00:30:40.125
Lucinha, Vicenza. Vicenza, Lucinha.

454
00:30:40.208 --> 00:30:41.291
-Hi.
-How are you?

455
00:30:41.375 --> 00:30:42.916
[Cadu] She's staying here with us.

456
00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:45.541
Oh my, is there going to be
a costume party?

457
00:30:45.625 --> 00:30:47.083
No, this is what I wear.

458
00:30:47.166 --> 00:30:50.375
Aw, you're so cute.

459
00:30:51.083 --> 00:30:52.916
You're a real hippie, huh?

460
00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:55.208
[gasps] You're hooking up with Cadu, huh?

461
00:30:55.291 --> 00:30:59.125
-No, Lucinha. It's not that. She…
-Shush! Just be grateful, okay?

462
00:30:59.208 --> 00:31:01.458
This guy here can't flirt
to save his life.

463
00:31:01.541 --> 00:31:04.583
So, seeing Little Cadu with someone
is a miracle.

464
00:31:04.666 --> 00:31:07.333
It's a sign that things work out
when we have enough faith.

465
00:31:07.416 --> 00:31:08.583
Hallelujah, Lord!

466
00:31:08.666 --> 00:31:10.416
Have you ever seen a rave
with poor lighting?

467
00:31:11.791 --> 00:31:13.958
No, of course you haven't!
Come on, man.

468
00:31:14.750 --> 00:31:17.750
No, look,  I don't care!
I need more lights, period!

469
00:31:17.833 --> 00:31:20.125
Hey, Betina. Look what I made.

470
00:31:20.208 --> 00:31:22.125
Oh, it's looking good!

471
00:31:22.208 --> 00:31:23.416
-I like it.
-Thanks.

472
00:31:23.500 --> 00:31:24.916
-You did this?
-Mm-hmm.

473
00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:26.750
Oh, that looks pretty!

474
00:31:26.833 --> 00:31:27.708
Vicenza.

475
00:31:28.208 --> 00:31:29.541
Someone's here to see you.

476
00:31:30.375 --> 00:31:31.875
You think we can talk?

477
00:31:34.208 --> 00:31:38.208
You have every reason to be mad at me.

478
00:31:40.791 --> 00:31:42.166
I'm glad you know that.

479
00:31:42.833 --> 00:31:43.958
Yeah…

480
00:31:45.333 --> 00:31:48.125
I shouldn't ever
talk to you like that. Ever.

481
00:31:56.125 --> 00:32:00.000
Yeah… not that it could justify
how rude I was, you know,

482
00:32:00.541 --> 00:32:04.291
not even in the slightest,
of course, but my life's not…

483
00:32:05.125 --> 00:32:08.041
you know, really good right now.

484
00:32:09.375 --> 00:32:12.375
Actually, it's pretty bad right now.

485
00:32:13.708 --> 00:32:15.458
I've been, uh…

486
00:32:15.541 --> 00:32:18.583
I've been frustrated, I've been angry.

487
00:32:18.666 --> 00:32:21.375
It's been ages since I felt
any inspiration, I'm broke.

488
00:32:22.500 --> 00:32:24.291
I don't have anything.

489
00:32:25.250 --> 00:32:27.333
So, then I think I… I ended up…

490
00:32:27.416 --> 00:32:29.166
taking it out on you,

491
00:32:29.250 --> 00:32:31.583
with all this stuff I'm dealing with.

492
00:32:33.916 --> 00:32:34.750
Forgive me.

493
00:32:38.625 --> 00:32:40.750
I have to apologize to you as well.

494
00:32:41.416 --> 00:32:43.500
I shouldn't have messed with your things.

495
00:32:44.083 --> 00:32:46.375
Yeah, but they actually said
they miss you.

496
00:32:48.125 --> 00:32:49.083
My things.

497
00:32:49.166 --> 00:32:51.041
[both chuckle]

498
00:32:52.333 --> 00:32:54.500
Seriously, will you forgive me?

499
00:32:56.000 --> 00:32:56.916
Of course.

500
00:32:58.666 --> 00:33:02.083
I want to just start over from scratch.

501
00:33:02.166 --> 00:33:04.333
You know, just pretend nothing happened

502
00:33:04.416 --> 00:33:06.375
and we just start over.

503
00:33:08.416 --> 00:33:10.375
-Wanna go for a walk with me?
-A walk?

504
00:33:10.458 --> 00:33:12.166
-Yeah!
-Aw, how cute!

505
00:33:12.250 --> 00:33:13.791
Let's do it. Let's go for a walk.

506
00:33:13.875 --> 00:33:15.000
-For real?
-Mm-hmm.

507
00:33:15.083 --> 00:33:16.750
-So go change.
-Okay.

508
00:33:22.625 --> 00:33:24.875
-[Paco] Your mother is really special.
-I know.

509
00:33:24.958 --> 00:33:26.041
[Paco] Very special.

510
00:33:26.125 --> 00:33:29.750
I remember her well.
She came to Santa Teresa for a retreat

511
00:33:29.833 --> 00:33:31.333
and stayed through Carnival.

512
00:33:31.416 --> 00:33:35.333
We weren't together for long.
We hung out for like three weeks.

513
00:33:35.416 --> 00:33:36.500
Not even a month.

514
00:33:36.583 --> 00:33:39.375
She really loved
this place where I'm taking you.

515
00:33:40.416 --> 00:33:43.000
-And I think you'll like it too.
-[chuckles]

516
00:33:49.958 --> 00:33:51.041
Oh!

517
00:33:54.041 --> 00:33:55.125
Ah!

518
00:33:56.500 --> 00:33:58.166
-That's amazing.
-[chuckles]

519
00:33:58.250 --> 00:34:01.208
So tell me, what are you planning to do,

520
00:34:01.291 --> 00:34:03.416
with all this
"might be your father" thing?

521
00:34:03.500 --> 00:34:05.625
I told you.
I just want to get to know you.

522
00:34:06.208 --> 00:34:08.500
-That's what we're doing now, right?
-Yes.

523
00:34:08.583 --> 00:34:10.625
-That's why we're here.
-Mm-hmm.

524
00:34:11.750 --> 00:34:13.333
-Do you have any kids?
-No.

525
00:34:14.458 --> 00:34:16.333
-I've never wanted any.
-Why?

526
00:34:16.416 --> 00:34:19.291
Raising a child is serious business,
it's really complex.

527
00:34:19.958 --> 00:34:22.375
I never thought I was
cut out to be a father.

528
00:34:23.291 --> 00:34:26.500
You know, I never thought
I would be responsible enough

529
00:34:26.583 --> 00:34:27.750
to raise someone.

530
00:34:27.833 --> 00:34:30.000
It's pretty responsible of you
to say that.

531
00:34:30.083 --> 00:34:31.250
[chuckles]

532
00:34:32.333 --> 00:34:36.291
It's so crazy, isn't it? The Universe
drops a daughter on you out of nowhere.

533
00:34:36.375 --> 00:34:37.500
[both chuckle]

534
00:34:39.250 --> 00:34:41.291
It's so crazy. Insane.

535
00:34:42.333 --> 00:34:43.708
But I'm really digging it.

536
00:34:45.333 --> 00:34:46.166
Majorly.

537
00:34:48.875 --> 00:34:50.125
[Paco groans]

538
00:35:04.208 --> 00:35:07.166
I've always dreamt of eating
a nice burger with some soda.

539
00:35:07.250 --> 00:35:08.708
[chuckling]

540
00:35:08.791 --> 00:35:11.458
-How come? Have you never had one?
-Mm-mm.

541
00:35:11.583 --> 00:35:12.708
I've never eaten meat.

542
00:35:13.625 --> 00:35:16.916
[groans] Why didn't you say something?
We could've gone somewhere else.

543
00:35:17.000 --> 00:35:18.208
Mm-mm!

544
00:35:18.291 --> 00:35:19.708
I really wanted to try it.

545
00:35:20.583 --> 00:35:22.333
Your favorite hamburger.

546
00:35:22.416 --> 00:35:25.166
And when you were talking about it,
you were so excited,

547
00:35:25.250 --> 00:35:26.916
I didn't want to disappoint you.

548
00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:29.125
-Is it good?
-It tastes like armpits.

549
00:35:29.208 --> 00:35:31.083
-[chuckling]
-But it's good, isn't it?

550
00:35:32.291 --> 00:35:33.125
Look.

551
00:35:33.208 --> 00:35:36.250
After this, I'll take you
to see the statue of Drummond.

552
00:35:36.875 --> 00:35:40.208
Do you know where it is?
In Copacabana, near Tower Six…

553
00:35:40.291 --> 00:35:42.166
[Vicenza grunting]

554
00:35:42.250 --> 00:35:43.916
-[Paco] Are you okay?
-No!

555
00:35:44.000 --> 00:35:45.250
But I will be!

556
00:35:45.875 --> 00:35:46.791
[Paco] Vicenza?

557
00:35:46.875 --> 00:35:48.291
[Vicenza retching]

558
00:35:48.375 --> 00:35:49.333
Vicenza?

559
00:35:50.291 --> 00:35:52.791
-[Vicenza] Yeah?
-Are... you okay?

560
00:35:52.875 --> 00:35:54.416
[Vicenza burping] No!

561
00:35:58.083 --> 00:36:00.125
[Paco] I really don't have anything.

562
00:36:00.208 --> 00:36:02.708
Only water, expired yogurt, eggs and soda.

563
00:36:02.791 --> 00:36:05.541
You seriously don't have anything
to make tea in this house?

564
00:36:05.625 --> 00:36:07.625
-Yeah, sorry.
-Peppermint?

565
00:36:07.708 --> 00:36:10.750
Or lemongrass? Or ginger? Even Chamomile?

566
00:36:12.958 --> 00:36:14.958
-Tell me more.
-About teas?

567
00:36:15.041 --> 00:36:15.958
Yeah.

568
00:36:16.750 --> 00:36:17.791
Um…

569
00:36:18.791 --> 00:36:20.000
Fennel?

570
00:36:20.083 --> 00:36:23.625
Or bilberry? Or chaga? Or hibiscus?

571
00:36:29.750 --> 00:36:30.833
Are you going to paint?

572
00:36:34.458 --> 00:36:36.500
[Paco] Keep talking, keep talking.

573
00:36:37.750 --> 00:36:38.625
Mulungu.

574
00:36:38.708 --> 00:36:40.000
Or Guaçatonga!

575
00:36:41.291 --> 00:36:42.875
Espinheira santa!

576
00:36:47.458 --> 00:36:49.666
-Star anise.
-Star anise.

577
00:37:08.583 --> 00:37:09.416
Here.

578
00:37:10.291 --> 00:37:12.416
See how tidying up the place helped?

579
00:37:13.375 --> 00:37:16.375
Ah. You think that tidying up the place
is what helped me?

580
00:37:16.458 --> 00:37:18.541
[laughing]

581
00:37:19.833 --> 00:37:20.708
Mmm!

582
00:37:22.375 --> 00:37:23.625
You wanna paint together?

583
00:37:24.166 --> 00:37:26.875
-I've never painted with someone else.
-Me neither.

584
00:37:26.958 --> 00:37:27.791
Wanna try?

585
00:37:28.458 --> 00:37:30.291
-Let's do it.
-Come on, come on!

586
00:37:36.708 --> 00:37:39.416
["Nessa Paz Eu Vou" by Tiago Iorc playing]

587
00:37:58.875 --> 00:38:00.958
A stroke just like this.

588
00:38:01.041 --> 00:38:03.250
Release your arms.

589
00:38:29.375 --> 00:38:30.875
-It's great.
-Mm-hmm.

590
00:38:32.333 --> 00:38:34.916
Do you have a boyfriend
at the Cosmic Universe?

591
00:38:37.291 --> 00:38:38.375
Girlfriend?

592
00:38:41.250 --> 00:38:42.083
A partner?

593
00:38:42.166 --> 00:38:43.791
-[Vicenza chuckling]
-Huh?

594
00:38:44.500 --> 00:38:45.333
No?

595
00:38:45.416 --> 00:38:46.958
Let's go back to painting.

596
00:38:51.625 --> 00:38:52.583
Painting.

597
00:39:02.250 --> 00:39:03.708
[sighs]

598
00:39:23.291 --> 00:39:24.458
[exhales]

599
00:39:34.041 --> 00:39:35.416
Cadu!

600
00:39:35.500 --> 00:39:37.666
-Cadu!
-Yeah. What's up, Vicenza?

601
00:39:38.500 --> 00:39:40.666
I found something
that might change my life.

602
00:39:41.208 --> 00:39:42.458
Do you know this guy?

603
00:39:42.541 --> 00:39:43.583
[Arthur] Of course!

604
00:39:43.666 --> 00:39:46.375
It's Giovanne. He used to live here.

605
00:39:46.458 --> 00:39:48.916
I mean, he's been gone
for a long time, but…

606
00:39:49.625 --> 00:39:52.250
but he and Paco were close friends.

607
00:39:52.333 --> 00:39:53.708
Do you remember his last name?

608
00:39:53.791 --> 00:39:55.791
His surname was Italian.

609
00:39:56.791 --> 00:39:58.833
Pavaro… No, not Pavarotti.

610
00:39:58.916 --> 00:40:01.041
It starts with B… Ah!

611
00:40:01.708 --> 00:40:03.166
-Benizatto!
-Benizatto.

612
00:40:03.250 --> 00:40:06.458
"Giovanne Benizatto with double T,"
as he used to say. That's him.

613
00:40:06.541 --> 00:40:08.416
And you never heard anything from him?

614
00:40:08.500 --> 00:40:09.666
Look, it's been a while.

615
00:40:10.333 --> 00:40:12.166
Someone once told me he was working

616
00:40:12.250 --> 00:40:14.833
in the financial market,
dealing with stocks and stuff.

617
00:40:14.916 --> 00:40:16.791
So, he might work at Leader Bank?

618
00:40:16.875 --> 00:40:18.583
Yes. If he's not the owner.

619
00:40:18.666 --> 00:40:20.291
So that's it. I found it.

620
00:40:21.250 --> 00:40:22.666
I found where he works.

621
00:40:24.458 --> 00:40:26.583
-Can you take me there?
-[Cadu] Sure.

622
00:40:26.666 --> 00:40:27.666
Thank you, Pop.

623
00:40:27.750 --> 00:40:29.375
-God bless you both.
-Thanks.

624
00:40:32.750 --> 00:40:34.958
[Cadu] Vicenza,
if you don't mind me asking,

625
00:40:35.041 --> 00:40:37.500
why is it so important
for you to meet this Giovanne?

626
00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:41.500
-Because he could be my father.
-Ah.

627
00:40:42.375 --> 00:40:44.541
I could have sworn Paco was my father.

628
00:40:44.625 --> 00:40:46.375
Wait a minute. Paco?

629
00:40:47.083 --> 00:40:50.125
So, I found a picture
that my mother's been hiding

630
00:40:50.208 --> 00:40:53.416
since Carnival of 2002, of her and Paco.

631
00:40:53.500 --> 00:40:55.125
That's the reason I came here.

632
00:40:55.208 --> 00:40:58.083
Then I found out
Giovanne was also with my mom

633
00:40:58.166 --> 00:41:00.041
during the same Carnival.

634
00:41:00.125 --> 00:41:03.000
And they were even kissing
in the photo I found of them.

635
00:41:03.541 --> 00:41:07.083
While in the picture of my mom with Paco,
they're just hugging.

636
00:41:08.333 --> 00:41:09.833
I have to meet him, Cadu.

637
00:41:09.916 --> 00:41:13.625
You will. You will meet him.
Trust me, I promise I will help you.

638
00:41:14.875 --> 00:41:15.958
It'll be an honor.

639
00:41:24.375 --> 00:41:26.500
Did you think about
how you're gonna get in?

640
00:41:26.583 --> 00:41:28.458
[Vicenza] Why? Can't I just walk in?

641
00:41:28.541 --> 00:41:31.083
No, there's-- there's security and…

642
00:41:31.166 --> 00:41:34.291
-Also, there's a little--
-Cadu, I'm following my heart. Relax.

643
00:41:34.375 --> 00:41:36.291
When I do that, things work out for me. 

644
00:41:36.375 --> 00:41:38.333
Always. In a very crazy way.

645
00:41:38.416 --> 00:41:40.333
But it shouldn't go wrong now, right?

646
00:41:40.916 --> 00:41:41.750
Right.

647
00:41:44.625 --> 00:41:46.541
Good morning. Name, please.

648
00:41:46.625 --> 00:41:50.125
Vicenza Shakti Pravananda
Sarahara Oxalá Zalala da Silva.

649
00:41:51.416 --> 00:41:53.291
Silva. Okay.

650
00:41:53.375 --> 00:41:54.583
Uh, where are you going?

651
00:41:54.666 --> 00:41:56.708
Uh, I'm heading to Leader Bank.

652
00:41:56.791 --> 00:41:57.833
Okay, which floor?

653
00:41:59.250 --> 00:42:00.416
No idea.

654
00:42:00.500 --> 00:42:02.625
What? How can I announce you're here?

655
00:42:02.708 --> 00:42:04.166
Could you not announce it?

656
00:42:04.250 --> 00:42:06.500
Of course not. I'm being paid to announce.

657
00:42:09.916 --> 00:42:14.708
Uh… Ma'am, the person
I came to see doesn't know I exist,

658
00:42:14.791 --> 00:42:17.041
and I didn't know
about his existence either.

659
00:42:17.125 --> 00:42:19.000
-Do you understand?
-No.

660
00:42:20.250 --> 00:42:21.958
I came here to meet my father.

661
00:42:22.041 --> 00:42:23.000
[gasps]

662
00:42:27.083 --> 00:42:28.916
-What's his name?
-Giovanne Benizatto.

663
00:42:29.000 --> 00:42:30.125
[keys clacking]

664
00:42:30.208 --> 00:42:31.333
Do you know him?

665
00:42:31.958 --> 00:42:33.291
I don't know him.

666
00:42:33.875 --> 00:42:35.708
But you are going to!

667
00:42:35.791 --> 00:42:36.875
[woman sniffs]

668
00:42:36.958 --> 00:42:38.375
-Picture.
-With me?

669
00:42:38.458 --> 00:42:39.541
No, here.

670
00:42:39.625 --> 00:42:40.916
[chuckles]

671
00:42:41.583 --> 00:42:42.416
Great.

672
00:42:46.208 --> 00:42:49.166
Good luck to you.
On the tenth floor, room 1002.

673
00:42:49.250 --> 00:42:50.583
In gratitude.

674
00:42:50.666 --> 00:42:52.583
-In gratitude right back at ya!
-[chuckles]

675
00:42:55.708 --> 00:42:57.083
-[turnstile clacks]
-[beeps]

676
00:42:57.625 --> 00:42:58.666
Can I help you?

677
00:43:00.208 --> 00:43:01.375
[Vicenza] Um…

678
00:43:02.958 --> 00:43:04.166
[beeps]

679
00:43:05.583 --> 00:43:06.500
Thank you.

680
00:43:06.583 --> 00:43:07.541
No problem.

681
00:43:16.083 --> 00:43:17.500
[female voice] Going up.

682
00:43:17.583 --> 00:43:18.416
Ten!

683
00:43:24.291 --> 00:43:25.208
Ten!

684
00:43:29.666 --> 00:43:30.916
[beeps]

685
00:43:33.583 --> 00:43:34.916
[female voice] First floor.

686
00:43:44.583 --> 00:43:45.583
Ten!

687
00:43:48.458 --> 00:43:49.750
[man] Ten.

688
00:43:49.833 --> 00:43:50.750
[elevator dings]

689
00:43:54.666 --> 00:43:55.916
[female voice] Going up.

690
00:43:57.583 --> 00:44:00.125
Wow, this is cool. This box flies.

691
00:44:00.625 --> 00:44:02.166
[elevator dings]

692
00:44:19.625 --> 00:44:20.458
Can I help you?

693
00:44:21.458 --> 00:44:24.416
-Hi. I'm looking for Giovanne Benizatto.
-Over there.

694
00:44:24.500 --> 00:44:26.958
I know. I understand, Mr. Victor.

695
00:44:27.041 --> 00:44:30.958
Lower your voice when you talk to me.
I told you, you could lose money.

696
00:44:31.041 --> 00:44:33.583
[shouting] Lower your voice to talk to me!

697
00:44:36.166 --> 00:44:38.291
-Can I help you? Looking for someone?
-You.

698
00:44:38.375 --> 00:44:41.083
-For me? And who are you?
-Vicenza.

699
00:44:42.833 --> 00:44:44.333
I'm Raion's daughter.

700
00:44:45.333 --> 00:44:47.333
-[scoffs] Raion?
-Mm-hmm.

701
00:44:47.416 --> 00:44:49.708
So long since I heard from your mom.

702
00:44:52.708 --> 00:44:53.541
Uh, have a seat.

703
00:44:56.166 --> 00:44:58.000
And how is she?

704
00:44:58.083 --> 00:45:00.833
Oh, you know, she's good.
So, I came here because--

705
00:45:00.916 --> 00:45:04.083
You're in a bad financial situation
and you came here for advice.

706
00:45:04.166 --> 00:45:05.375
[both chuckle]

707
00:45:05.458 --> 00:45:08.708
Listen, you know I charge
a small fortune to do this,

708
00:45:08.791 --> 00:45:10.875
but for you, I'll do it for free.

709
00:45:10.958 --> 00:45:11.791
For Raion.

710
00:45:11.875 --> 00:45:15.333
You know I had a little fling
with your mom, right? [chuckles]

711
00:45:15.416 --> 00:45:18.208
-Oh, wow.
-Let's start.

712
00:45:18.291 --> 00:45:19.500
What's your name, cutie?

713
00:45:19.583 --> 00:45:23.500
Uh, Vicenza Shakti Pravananda Oxalá
Sarahara Zalala da Silva.

714
00:45:24.291 --> 00:45:25.708
Silva.

715
00:45:25.791 --> 00:45:27.750
Mother's name. Raion…

716
00:45:27.833 --> 00:45:29.125
-Silva.
-Silva.

717
00:45:30.416 --> 00:45:31.250
Father's name?

718
00:45:32.500 --> 00:45:33.833
I don't have a father.

719
00:45:34.375 --> 00:45:35.416
Okay.

720
00:45:35.500 --> 00:45:37.041
Date of birth?

721
00:45:37.125 --> 00:45:39.291
Uh, November 8th, 2002.

722
00:45:39.916 --> 00:45:42.000
The same year
you happened to meet my mom.

723
00:45:42.083 --> 00:45:43.625
[chuckling]

724
00:45:43.708 --> 00:45:45.750
You could be my daughter. [chuckles]

725
00:45:45.833 --> 00:45:47.208
[chuckles]

726
00:45:47.875 --> 00:45:49.208
[sighs]

727
00:45:56.500 --> 00:45:58.083
You could be my daughter?

728
00:46:02.208 --> 00:46:04.375
-That's why you're here?
-Yes.

729
00:46:07.125 --> 00:46:08.416
-Daughter?
-Daughter.

730
00:46:10.500 --> 00:46:12.000
-Daughter.
-Daughter.

731
00:46:14.250 --> 00:46:15.250
Daughter!

732
00:46:30.875 --> 00:46:31.750
[grunts]

733
00:46:57.708 --> 00:47:00.958
I, uh… I think that…
I think that we need to talk, right?

734
00:47:03.833 --> 00:47:07.250
["Cabelo de Anjo"
by Melim &amp; Lulu Santos playing]

735
00:47:16.750 --> 00:47:19.250
Do you wanna grab something to eat?
Are you hungry?

736
00:47:19.333 --> 00:47:21.333
I'm actually always hungry.

737
00:47:21.416 --> 00:47:23.583
But I don't want to eat at a restaurant.

738
00:47:23.666 --> 00:47:25.541
A homemade meal would be awesome.

739
00:47:26.625 --> 00:47:29.875
So I know exactly where to take you.
Come here.

740
00:47:33.208 --> 00:47:34.208
Taxi!

741
00:47:37.750 --> 00:47:38.916
[Vicenza] Hi!

742
00:47:49.833 --> 00:47:51.041
Wow!

743
00:47:58.791 --> 00:48:00.333
[Giovanne] Can you give me a hand?

744
00:48:00.416 --> 00:48:01.833
-Mm-hmm.
-Here you go.

745
00:48:05.708 --> 00:48:06.666
[sighs]

746
00:48:07.916 --> 00:48:09.083
It's funny.

747
00:48:09.166 --> 00:48:11.291
My stepsons never cooked with me.

748
00:48:11.375 --> 00:48:12.750
I mean, ex-stepsons.

749
00:48:13.500 --> 00:48:15.916
And have you ever invited them
to cook with you?

750
00:48:16.000 --> 00:48:16.916
Yeah.

751
00:48:17.000 --> 00:48:18.708
I mean, I think I have.

752
00:48:18.791 --> 00:48:20.708
-[chuckles]
-Got it.

753
00:48:20.791 --> 00:48:21.958
Okay. Careful here.

754
00:48:24.416 --> 00:48:26.125
How many stepsons do you have?

755
00:48:26.208 --> 00:48:28.083
Two. Guilherme and Rael.

756
00:48:28.166 --> 00:48:29.083
Are they nice?

757
00:48:29.166 --> 00:48:31.875
They're the coolest guys I've ever met.

758
00:48:31.958 --> 00:48:34.125
-How long have you been divorced?
-Two years.

759
00:48:34.208 --> 00:48:35.375
Mmm.

760
00:48:35.458 --> 00:48:38.166
-Are you still friends with their mother?
-With Marta?

761
00:48:39.333 --> 00:48:41.750
Yes, yes. Marta is…

762
00:48:41.833 --> 00:48:44.333
a good friend of mine.

763
00:48:44.416 --> 00:48:45.500
[both laughing]

764
00:48:51.375 --> 00:48:52.208
Thanks.

765
00:49:13.208 --> 00:49:16.541
[man] Ohm…

766
00:49:18.041 --> 00:49:20.666
The most important thing in life
is to breathe.

767
00:49:21.458 --> 00:49:23.250
Breath is peace, breath is water…

768
00:49:23.333 --> 00:49:27.083
Hear me out, don't you think it's crazy
for us to come all the way to India

769
00:49:27.166 --> 00:49:29.708
to watch a guy in Los Angeles
on a Skype call?

770
00:49:29.791 --> 00:49:32.041
He's not sweating like a pig over here.

771
00:49:32.666 --> 00:49:34.166
With these bugs.

772
00:49:35.708 --> 00:49:39.333
And we can't even kill the flies.
It's not spiritually evolved to kill them.

773
00:49:39.416 --> 00:49:41.208
-Shh!
-Shh!

774
00:49:41.291 --> 00:49:43.500
[man] Let's breathe like the beetle.

775
00:49:43.583 --> 00:49:46.083
Let's try! Hard! Very hard!

776
00:49:46.166 --> 00:49:47.208
[inhales]

777
00:49:47.791 --> 00:49:51.875
Ohm…

778
00:49:52.458 --> 00:49:55.166
Tell me, why did it take you so long
to look for me?

779
00:49:55.250 --> 00:49:58.916
Because my mom went to India,
so this was the first time I could escape.

780
00:49:59.000 --> 00:50:00.791
What do you mean, escape?

781
00:50:00.875 --> 00:50:03.291
Escape?
Your mom doesn't know you're here?

782
00:50:03.375 --> 00:50:04.583
Relax, relax.

783
00:50:04.666 --> 00:50:06.958
I came following my heart.
It's all good.

784
00:50:07.041 --> 00:50:09.500
No, it's not.
We'll have to call your mom right now!

785
00:50:09.583 --> 00:50:11.916
No way, I'm sorry. She's way out of reach.

786
00:50:12.625 --> 00:50:13.541
[scoffs]

787
00:50:19.500 --> 00:50:21.000
So you had to run away?

788
00:50:22.041 --> 00:50:24.208
Raion doesn't want you to meet me?

789
00:50:24.291 --> 00:50:27.208
Actually, she didn't want to talk
about you or anyone.

790
00:50:27.291 --> 00:50:31.625
All she said was, "It's not the time
for you to meet your father."

791
00:50:32.250 --> 00:50:34.458
-But it never was!
-I see.

792
00:50:34.541 --> 00:50:37.791
And you're sick and tired of not knowing
who your father is.

793
00:50:37.875 --> 00:50:38.833
Absolutely.

794
00:50:40.166 --> 00:50:41.000
Uh…

795
00:50:41.500 --> 00:50:43.041
Do you want a little more tea?

796
00:50:43.125 --> 00:50:46.125
No, thank you.
Actually, I think it's getting late.

797
00:50:46.208 --> 00:50:48.166
-I should go.
-No, stay a little more.

798
00:50:48.250 --> 00:50:49.625
It's raining.

799
00:50:49.708 --> 00:50:50.875
Where are you staying?

800
00:50:50.958 --> 00:50:53.583
At the headquarters of a troupe
in Santa Teresa.

801
00:50:53.666 --> 00:50:56.541
-The Naked Amoeba. Do you know it?
-Come on!

802
00:50:57.375 --> 00:50:58.875
I haven't been there in forever.

803
00:51:01.916 --> 00:51:03.625
Why don't we do this? Look…

804
00:51:03.708 --> 00:51:06.500
you sleep here tonight, in Rael's bedroom,

805
00:51:06.583 --> 00:51:09.750
and tomorrow morning,
before I go to work, I'll take you there.

806
00:51:17.041 --> 00:51:18.166
[phone pings]

807
00:51:49.625 --> 00:51:51.250
[curtains open]

808
00:51:51.375 --> 00:51:52.625
[woman] What's going on here?

809
00:51:52.708 --> 00:51:55.416
-Huh? What is this?
-Calm down. I can explain.

810
00:51:55.500 --> 00:51:57.541
Yeah, I think
you should explain, Giovanne.

811
00:51:57.625 --> 00:52:00.166
It's not every day we come to your house,

812
00:52:00.250 --> 00:52:02.583
and Rael finds Sleeping Beauty in his bed!

813
00:52:02.666 --> 00:52:04.416
Listen, this is Vicenza.

814
00:52:05.875 --> 00:52:07.000
She may be my daughter.

815
00:52:07.083 --> 00:52:08.875
What did you say, Giovanne?

816
00:52:09.458 --> 00:52:11.833
Your daughter, Giovanne?
She may be your daughter?

817
00:52:11.916 --> 00:52:13.000
-Daughter?
-Calm down!

818
00:52:13.083 --> 00:52:16.125
-[Marta] What do you mean?
-[Giovanne] I'll explain outside.

819
00:52:16.208 --> 00:52:17.833
Calm down! Stop yelling!

820
00:52:17.916 --> 00:52:20.458
-[Marta] I can't believe it!
-Are you going to live here?

821
00:52:20.541 --> 00:52:22.750
-Do you play Fortnite?
-[Rael] Or FIFA?

822
00:52:22.833 --> 00:52:24.250
Are you good at math?

823
00:52:24.333 --> 00:52:25.333
Uh…

824
00:52:25.416 --> 00:52:27.750
No, I'm not gonna live here.

825
00:52:27.833 --> 00:52:30.083
I don't know those games, and…

826
00:52:30.833 --> 00:52:32.791
-I'm really good at math.
-Yes!

827
00:52:32.875 --> 00:52:34.916
[Marta]
Don't disrespect me in front of the kids!

828
00:52:35.000 --> 00:52:36.208
[Giovanne] Stop yelling!

829
00:52:36.291 --> 00:52:39.208
[Marta] You can't seriously think
that girl is your child.

830
00:52:39.291 --> 00:52:40.333
How dumb are you?

831
00:52:40.416 --> 00:52:44.166
Uh, boys, I need to be alone for a bit
to get changed. Can you excuse me?

832
00:52:44.250 --> 00:52:45.125
-Sure.
-Mm-hmm.

833
00:52:45.208 --> 00:52:46.083
Thank you.

834
00:52:46.166 --> 00:52:47.583
[Marta and Giovanne arguing]

835
00:52:47.666 --> 00:52:49.666
-[Marta] Are you out of your mind?
-I talked to her!

836
00:52:49.750 --> 00:52:51.375
[Marta] Oh my God, wake up!

837
00:52:51.458 --> 00:52:55.291
Have you thought about the huge amount
of money you have in the bank?

838
00:52:55.375 --> 00:52:56.541
What about it?

839
00:52:56.625 --> 00:53:00.458
This girl is clearly just thinking
about taking all of your money!

840
00:53:00.541 --> 00:53:01.708
Stop! Lower your voice!

841
00:53:01.791 --> 00:53:03.500
I won't! You're driving me insane.

842
00:53:03.583 --> 00:53:06.291
-You're getting it all wrong.
-You're irresponsible!

843
00:53:06.375 --> 00:53:09.208
I don't regret divorcing you at all!

844
00:53:09.291 --> 00:53:11.000
I don't regret it either!

845
00:53:11.083 --> 00:53:13.625
I wasn't gonna sit there and hear
that woman question my character.

846
00:53:13.708 --> 00:53:15.750
Vicenza, I don't know why you care.

847
00:53:15.833 --> 00:53:17.791
Little does she know you're an angel.

848
00:53:17.875 --> 00:53:20.791
-Me? An angel? Really?
-Really.

849
00:53:20.875 --> 00:53:22.708
The most beautiful angel of all.

850
00:53:23.166 --> 00:53:24.416
-[chuckles]
-[phone buzzes]

851
00:53:24.500 --> 00:53:25.333
Oh!

852
00:53:28.958 --> 00:53:31.208
It's Paco. He wants to hang out with me.

853
00:53:31.291 --> 00:53:33.208
Are you gonna mention Giovanne?

854
00:53:35.000 --> 00:53:37.458
Oh, Cadu. I don't know.

855
00:53:37.541 --> 00:53:39.000
I don't want to hurt him.

856
00:53:39.083 --> 00:53:41.416
I'm absolutely sure if I tell him,
he'll be sad.

857
00:53:41.500 --> 00:53:44.291
And I don't want to be the person
that makes Paco sad.

858
00:53:44.375 --> 00:53:47.250
What about Giovanne?
You tell him about Paco then?

859
00:53:47.333 --> 00:53:48.916
He's so cool.

860
00:53:49.000 --> 00:53:51.500
Cadu, help me. I don't know what to do.

861
00:53:51.583 --> 00:53:54.541
-[Betina] Be careful.
-I think you should tell them the truth.

862
00:53:54.625 --> 00:53:56.291
You're crazy, right, Cadu?

863
00:53:56.375 --> 00:53:58.416
-So you were listening?
-Betina.

864
00:53:58.500 --> 00:54:02.208
Yeah, I was listening, okay?
I like a good gossip, I can't resist it.

865
00:54:02.291 --> 00:54:04.291
If I were you,
I wouldn't tell either of them.

866
00:54:04.375 --> 00:54:07.083
But I hate lying, Betina.
I don't even know how to.

867
00:54:07.166 --> 00:54:08.916
Oh, my sweet girl. Here me out.

868
00:54:09.000 --> 00:54:11.333
First, you're not gonna lie.
You're gonna omit.

869
00:54:11.416 --> 00:54:12.833
And second,

870
00:54:12.916 --> 00:54:16.250
why would you risk everything
you're creating with both of them? Huh?

871
00:54:16.333 --> 00:54:19.125
["Felicidade" by Marcelo Jeneci playing]

872
00:54:59.250 --> 00:55:01.250
[phone buzzes]

873
00:55:09.708 --> 00:55:10.583
[Vicenza] Here.

874
00:55:13.041 --> 00:55:16.333
I wanted to apologize.
For Marta, for myself.

875
00:55:16.416 --> 00:55:18.250
-I never imagined that…
-It's all right.

876
00:55:18.333 --> 00:55:20.541
Sometimes we say stuff
without thinking, right?

877
00:55:22.041 --> 00:55:23.583
But do you forgive me?

878
00:55:23.666 --> 00:55:26.333
I forgive you. Where are the boys?

879
00:55:26.416 --> 00:55:28.916
Uh, I asked them to come next week.

880
00:55:29.000 --> 00:55:30.750
I needed some time to be alone.

881
00:55:30.833 --> 00:55:34.541
My head is all over the place
with the chance of having a daughter.

882
00:55:35.625 --> 00:55:36.833
[chuckles]

883
00:55:36.916 --> 00:55:37.750
[kisses]

884
00:55:38.250 --> 00:55:39.500
[phone pings]

885
00:56:10.833 --> 00:56:11.875
[phone pings]

886
00:56:22.375 --> 00:56:23.625
Yes, it does.

887
00:56:24.500 --> 00:56:25.666
[phone pings]

888
00:56:36.375 --> 00:56:39.416
You're breathing right, huh, Mr. Paco!
You've learned!

889
00:56:40.083 --> 00:56:44.083
I have a very good teacher.
I'll give you her number later.

890
00:56:44.166 --> 00:56:45.708
[both chuckle]

891
00:56:45.791 --> 00:56:46.625
[kisses]

892
00:56:47.333 --> 00:56:48.166
[kisses]

893
00:56:50.625 --> 00:56:52.416
Align it with your shoulder.

894
00:56:52.500 --> 00:56:54.791
See, look. Same with this arm.

895
00:56:59.750 --> 00:57:00.916
[phone pings]

896
00:57:13.750 --> 00:57:15.458
Smell. Try it.

897
00:57:54.958 --> 00:57:58.250
Vi, I hope it's okay to ask,
but are you not telling Paco or Giovanne?

898
00:57:58.333 --> 00:57:59.791
[groans] I can't do it, Cadu.

899
00:57:59.875 --> 00:58:01.666
I don't want to hurt them, you know?

900
00:58:01.750 --> 00:58:05.083
I see. And what does your heart tell you?
You always listen to it.

901
00:58:05.166 --> 00:58:07.416
Sometimes my heart is sure it's Paco,

902
00:58:07.500 --> 00:58:09.500
but then it thinks it's Giovanne.

903
00:58:09.583 --> 00:58:11.500
Then why don't you take a DNA test?

904
00:58:11.583 --> 00:58:14.125
That'll do it. You know
what a DNA test is, don't you?

905
00:58:14.208 --> 00:58:15.583
Of course I do, Cadu!

906
00:58:15.666 --> 00:58:18.208
I don't live under a rock.
But doesn't it cost a fortune?

907
00:58:18.291 --> 00:58:19.958
No, no. Not anymore, I guess.

908
00:58:20.041 --> 00:58:22.708
It did in the past.
But it's pretty cheap nowadays,

909
00:58:22.791 --> 00:58:25.166
so everyone can do it.
I think there's a website…

910
00:58:25.250 --> 00:58:26.666
No, it's an app. No, a website.

911
00:58:26.750 --> 00:58:29.083
You put in all the info. Check it out.

912
00:58:29.166 --> 00:58:34.000
You just need to collect a few things,
like blood, saliva, hair…

913
00:58:35.375 --> 00:58:36.291
See? You just…

914
00:58:37.166 --> 00:58:38.000
Vi!

915
00:58:39.458 --> 00:58:41.041
Vi! Careful, careful!

916
00:58:41.125 --> 00:58:42.833
-When you get to the top, jump.
-Jump?

917
00:58:42.916 --> 00:58:44.500
No, not this way, that way.

918
00:58:44.583 --> 00:58:47.833
When you get there, you jump.
Wait, I'll help you. Hold on.

919
00:58:48.416 --> 00:58:50.083
-I'm almost there.
-Hold on, yeah.

920
00:58:50.166 --> 00:58:51.375
Jump. There we go.

921
00:58:51.458 --> 00:58:53.333
-[Vicenza] Oh, that's cool!
-[Cadu] Sorry.

922
00:59:00.791 --> 00:59:02.166
-[Cadu] Vi!
-There's another one!

923
00:59:02.750 --> 00:59:03.708
[Cadu] Vicenza, wait!

924
00:59:06.750 --> 00:59:08.166
Vi! Okay, calm down, I know.

925
00:59:08.250 --> 00:59:11.208
It's an escalator, it's something new.
Listen, I found the website.

926
00:59:11.291 --> 00:59:14.833
It says here you just need
a sample of blood, hair or saliva,

927
00:59:14.916 --> 00:59:17.208
then you'll know
who's the biological father.

928
00:59:20.958 --> 00:59:22.375
Vicenza, no. Enough escalators.

929
00:59:29.708 --> 00:59:30.916
[Paco] Mmm.

930
00:59:33.041 --> 00:59:34.500
[slurping]

931
00:59:46.333 --> 00:59:48.250
[chatting indistinctly]

932
00:59:48.333 --> 00:59:49.500
[Giovanne] Gotcha.

933
00:59:49.583 --> 00:59:50.416
Thank you.

934
00:59:50.500 --> 00:59:51.416
Thank you.

935
00:59:51.500 --> 00:59:53.833
You should use this straw.
It's eco-friendly.

936
00:59:53.916 --> 00:59:54.750
Sounds good.

937
00:59:55.583 --> 00:59:56.416
Let's do this.

938
00:59:58.041 --> 00:59:59.041
Mmm.

939
00:59:59.125 --> 01:00:00.666
[slurping]

940
01:00:07.958 --> 01:00:10.583
Here, Cadu.
Everything we need for the DNA test.

941
01:00:10.666 --> 01:00:12.500
Awesome. I'll take care of it for you.

942
01:00:12.583 --> 01:00:13.583
Thank you.

943
01:00:13.666 --> 01:00:14.583
[kisses]

944
01:00:14.666 --> 01:00:16.875
-I don't know what I'd do without you.
-[chuckles]

945
01:00:16.958 --> 01:00:19.416
I don't know what I'm gonna do
when you go back home.

946
01:00:19.916 --> 01:00:22.541
You're the most special girl
I've ever met, you know?

947
01:00:22.625 --> 01:00:24.000
-[chuckles]
-Bro!

948
01:00:24.083 --> 01:00:26.458
Listen, it's urgent.
We need to promote the rave.

949
01:00:26.541 --> 01:00:27.750
Ticket sales are terrible,

950
01:00:27.833 --> 01:00:30.333
and we need money
to put the parade out there, right?

951
01:00:30.416 --> 01:00:32.291
Let's print flyers and distribute them.

952
01:00:32.375 --> 01:00:33.583
-Awesome.
-Okay.

953
01:00:33.666 --> 01:00:34.625
[Betina] Come on.

954
01:00:34.708 --> 01:00:36.708
[man vocalizing] Ohm.

955
01:00:41.083 --> 01:00:46.083
Ohm.

956
01:00:47.958 --> 01:00:53.375
Ohm.

957
01:00:55.625 --> 01:01:01.208
Ohm.

958
01:01:03.125 --> 01:01:08.541
Ohm.

959
01:01:10.291 --> 01:01:11.125
[shrieks]

960
01:01:11.208 --> 01:01:12.500
[all] Shh!

961
01:01:12.583 --> 01:01:14.000
My daughter's missing!

962
01:01:15.083 --> 01:01:16.416
You don't understand.

963
01:01:16.500 --> 01:01:18.291
My daughter. My daughter missing.

964
01:01:18.375 --> 01:01:19.333
[all] Shh!

965
01:01:19.416 --> 01:01:20.791
Guys, how insensitive!

966
01:01:20.875 --> 01:01:22.583
I expected more from you here!

967
01:01:22.666 --> 01:01:24.250
Holy moly.

968
01:01:24.333 --> 01:01:27.833
How can you expect me to be zen
after this kind of news? Holy cow!

969
01:01:31.916 --> 01:01:32.791
[Paco] Hey there!

970
01:01:33.291 --> 01:01:34.791
-Hey.
-Look what I brought.

971
01:01:35.375 --> 01:01:37.000
I'm gonna make you the juice.

972
01:01:37.083 --> 01:01:38.666
-Mmm!
-For you.

973
01:01:38.750 --> 01:01:39.708
[both chuckling]

974
01:01:40.500 --> 01:01:41.833
It's nice.

975
01:01:41.916 --> 01:01:42.833
[Vicenza] Thank you.

976
01:01:43.416 --> 01:01:44.250
Look.

977
01:01:44.333 --> 01:01:46.333
Amoeba party. Shall we?

978
01:01:47.291 --> 01:01:48.541
Really? You want to go?

979
01:01:48.625 --> 01:01:49.666
Why wouldn't I?

980
01:01:49.750 --> 01:01:50.958
I'm too old for it?

981
01:01:51.583 --> 01:01:53.500
[chuckles] Of course not, Paco.

982
01:01:53.583 --> 01:01:54.583
[chuckles]

983
01:01:55.875 --> 01:01:58.208
-Use a little more orange.
-You got it.

984
01:02:03.625 --> 01:02:04.583
[scoffs]

985
01:02:04.666 --> 01:02:08.000
There will be a party at your place,
and you don't even invite me, huh?

986
01:02:10.041 --> 01:02:10.875
Yeah…

987
01:02:10.958 --> 01:02:15.000
Giovanne, how on earth would I know
you're into electronic music?

988
01:02:15.708 --> 01:02:17.125
I don't like it.

989
01:02:17.208 --> 01:02:19.333
But I'm gonna love seeing
everyone else.

990
01:02:19.416 --> 01:02:21.000
Especially since you're there.

991
01:02:21.083 --> 01:02:21.916
Shall we?

992
01:02:22.583 --> 01:02:24.208
[keys clacking]

993
01:02:24.333 --> 01:02:26.833
We shall! Sure, we'll go!

994
01:02:26.916 --> 01:02:28.666
Just bought the tickets.

995
01:02:28.750 --> 01:02:30.000
Mmm.

996
01:02:30.083 --> 01:02:31.333
[all sigh]

997
01:02:31.416 --> 01:02:34.000
Guys, I really need your help with this.

998
01:02:34.583 --> 01:02:36.166
I'll try to summarize it, okay?

999
01:02:36.250 --> 01:02:38.125
So, I never had a father--

1000
01:02:38.208 --> 01:02:40.000
Oh, poor little baby girl!

1001
01:02:40.083 --> 01:02:41.166
…but now I have two.

1002
01:02:41.250 --> 01:02:43.000
-Wow, then life is good!
-[all laugh]

1003
01:02:43.083 --> 01:02:46.000
I'm crazy about them.
They're both really, really cool.

1004
01:02:46.083 --> 01:02:47.333
They even know each other.

1005
01:02:47.416 --> 01:02:51.083
But neither of them can know
the other could also be my dad.

1006
01:02:51.166 --> 01:02:52.875
And both are coming to our party.

1007
01:02:52.958 --> 01:02:55.375
-[all react]
-Holy cow, you're screwed, girl!

1008
01:02:55.458 --> 01:02:58.333
-Lucinha, girl, you're not helping.
-Sorry. I feel for her.

1009
01:02:58.416 --> 01:03:01.375
Okay, and what can we do
for them to not bump into each other?

1010
01:03:01.458 --> 01:03:05.500
[gasps] I got it! Why don't we ask
everyone to wear costumes to the rave?

1011
01:03:05.583 --> 01:03:06.958
Like rave meets Carnival?

1012
01:03:07.041 --> 01:03:09.291
-[all gasp]
-You're a genius! That's it!

1013
01:03:09.375 --> 01:03:11.583
We'll leave a chest with costumes
at the entrance

1014
01:03:11.666 --> 01:03:14.166
so if anyone doesn't bring a costume,
they just grab one.

1015
01:03:14.250 --> 01:03:16.791
-There's no excuse.
-Yeah! Masks, noses, wigs…

1016
01:03:16.875 --> 01:03:19.416
It'd make it harder
for them to recognize each other.

1017
01:03:19.500 --> 01:03:20.708
You rock, Lucinha.

1018
01:03:22.666 --> 01:03:24.375
[Lucinha] That one over there.

1019
01:03:24.458 --> 01:03:25.666
[indistinct chatter]

1020
01:03:25.750 --> 01:03:27.375
Yeah, that one on the right.

1021
01:03:27.458 --> 01:03:29.958
[Nando and Cadu arguing]

1022
01:03:30.041 --> 01:03:32.458
-I'm practicing!
-Why? You can't play it!

1023
01:03:32.541 --> 01:03:35.083
[Nando and Cadu continue arguing]

1024
01:03:35.166 --> 01:03:37.541
[woman] Beautiful!
Oh, these are all tangled!

1025
01:03:37.625 --> 01:03:40.250
Betina, help me out here!
Come help me, please!

1026
01:03:40.333 --> 01:03:43.166
Cadu is taking away my tuba!
I was practicing…

1027
01:03:43.250 --> 01:03:46.000
[overlapping chattering]

1028
01:03:46.708 --> 01:03:47.833
[chuckling]

1029
01:03:47.916 --> 01:03:49.291
[woman] Did you bring that?

1030
01:03:50.416 --> 01:03:52.375
♪ Baby, you should know the truth ♪

1031
01:03:52.458 --> 01:03:54.208
♪ I'm not leaving without you ♪

1032
01:03:54.291 --> 01:03:55.875
♪You got me feeling so cool ♪

1033
01:03:55.958 --> 01:03:57.750
♪ All night I'll be lovin' you… ♪

1034
01:03:57.833 --> 01:04:00.458
[upbeat dance music playing]

1035
01:04:01.458 --> 01:04:03.458
Yes! With a cat costume!

1036
01:04:06.750 --> 01:04:08.250
Good job on the costume, bro!

1037
01:04:08.333 --> 01:04:10.166
[all laughing]

1038
01:04:10.250 --> 01:04:11.875
Guys, the party is packed!

1039
01:04:11.958 --> 01:04:14.250
You guys'll be able to parade
with the troupe!

1040
01:04:14.333 --> 01:04:16.125
We'll be able to parade with the troupe!

1041
01:04:16.208 --> 01:04:17.625
I told you it would work, guys!

1042
01:04:17.708 --> 01:04:19.541
[both chuckling]

1043
01:04:19.625 --> 01:04:21.916
-[Lucinha] Betina, come here!
-Whoa, hold on a sec!

1044
01:04:22.000 --> 01:04:24.208
-I'm gonna show you something. Come.
-Wait.

1045
01:04:28.458 --> 01:04:30.166
Vicenza! Vicenza!

1046
01:04:30.250 --> 01:04:32.083
[both chuckling]

1047
01:04:34.500 --> 01:04:36.541
I was dying to see you, I have great news.

1048
01:04:36.625 --> 01:04:37.875
Seriously? Go ahead!

1049
01:04:37.958 --> 01:04:41.208
My art dealer just told me
we closed a deal on an art exhibit

1050
01:04:41.291 --> 01:04:43.208
of my latest works in New York.

1051
01:04:43.291 --> 01:04:44.666
-No! Wow!
-Yeah!

1052
01:04:44.750 --> 01:04:46.708
That's awesome! [chuckling]

1053
01:04:46.791 --> 01:04:49.708
It's all thanks to you.
You inspired me to start painting again.

1054
01:04:49.791 --> 01:04:53.041
Come on, it was nothing.
Congratulations… Paco!

1055
01:04:54.375 --> 01:04:56.583
-You're coming with me, right?
-To New York?

1056
01:04:56.666 --> 01:04:58.791
It wouldn't make sense for me to go alone.

1057
01:04:58.875 --> 01:05:01.166
Uh, of course I'll go! When are you going?

1058
01:05:01.250 --> 01:05:02.375
February 9th.

1059
01:05:04.250 --> 01:05:05.583
You okay?

1060
01:05:05.666 --> 01:05:08.333
It's just 'cause
the Amoeba parade is on the 9th.

1061
01:05:08.416 --> 01:05:10.958
And, I mean, I helped with the flyers,

1062
01:05:11.041 --> 01:05:13.500
I sewed the banner,
I helped with the party.

1063
01:05:13.583 --> 01:05:16.916
I'm doing all I can to get it out there
and to make it great, you know?

1064
01:05:17.000 --> 01:05:17.833
Of course.

1065
01:05:18.750 --> 01:05:22.375
Of course. You're happy, right?
Because you helped organize everything,

1066
01:05:22.458 --> 01:05:23.500
so you're happy.

1067
01:05:25.041 --> 01:05:26.166
Are we good?

1068
01:05:26.250 --> 01:05:29.375
Of course. We're good.
If you're happy, I'm happy too.

1069
01:05:29.916 --> 01:05:31.041
Thank you.

1070
01:05:32.500 --> 01:05:33.833
[muted] It's Giovanne!

1071
01:05:33.916 --> 01:05:36.208
Uh, Paco,
I'm gonna go deal with something.

1072
01:05:36.291 --> 01:05:39.458
Take a look around, enjoy the party.
I'll be right back, okay?

1073
01:05:39.541 --> 01:05:40.791
Woo-hoo!

1074
01:05:41.375 --> 01:05:43.083
Hey, Paco!

1075
01:05:43.166 --> 01:05:44.333
Oh, hey, Luana!

1076
01:05:44.416 --> 01:05:46.333
It's Lucinha, Paco!

1077
01:05:49.041 --> 01:05:51.625
Vicenza! You look incredible!

1078
01:05:51.708 --> 01:05:53.375
Thank you, Giovanne!

1079
01:05:53.458 --> 01:05:55.291
-You too.
-So, what do you think?

1080
01:05:55.375 --> 01:05:58.750
-We could add some stuff to it. Look.
-Yeah?

1081
01:05:59.333 --> 01:06:00.541
-This one?
-Mm-hmm.

1082
01:06:00.625 --> 01:06:02.500
Okay, okay, okay.

1083
01:06:02.583 --> 01:06:04.875
Here-- Oh, boy!
I think you're overdoing it.

1084
01:06:04.958 --> 01:06:06.250
[both chuckling]

1085
01:06:06.333 --> 01:06:08.375
So? How about now?

1086
01:06:08.458 --> 01:06:10.083
Ta-da! Do I look great or what?

1087
01:06:10.166 --> 01:06:11.083
Awesome!

1088
01:06:11.166 --> 01:06:14.708
I look like someone who's going to Disney
with his stepsons for the first time.

1089
01:06:14.791 --> 01:06:17.291
-[gasps] That's incredible news!
-Will you come with us?

1090
01:06:17.375 --> 01:06:19.458
-To Disney World? For real?
-Yeah!

1091
01:06:19.541 --> 01:06:21.958
-Oh, my God! Of course! Wow!
-[chuckling]

1092
01:06:22.041 --> 01:06:24.041
-When will you go?
-February 9th.

1093
01:06:24.625 --> 01:06:26.083
[chuckling nervously] Um…

1094
01:06:26.166 --> 01:06:27.708
[muted] Paco is here!

1095
01:06:29.291 --> 01:06:31.125
-Nando!
-What's up?

1096
01:06:31.208 --> 01:06:32.833
You scared me, Vicenza.

1097
01:06:32.916 --> 01:06:36.458
Uh… um… Nando, this is Giovanne.

1098
01:06:36.541 --> 01:06:37.791
My, uh, friend.

1099
01:06:38.375 --> 01:06:40.708
Giovanne, this is Nando.
He's the troupe's, uh…

1100
01:06:40.791 --> 01:06:42.583
I'm the main musician of the troupe.

1101
01:06:42.666 --> 01:06:44.333
-I play all the instruments.
-Uh…

1102
01:06:44.416 --> 01:06:46.250
-Giovanne adores music.
-I do?

1103
01:06:46.333 --> 01:06:48.333
-You like music?
-I mean, I do, but…

1104
01:06:48.416 --> 01:06:49.875
Play for him. [chuckling]

1105
01:06:49.958 --> 01:06:52.333
You know our master?
The master! This one dude…

1106
01:06:52.416 --> 01:06:54.875
-Yeah, a master for sure.
-A classic, right?

1107
01:06:55.791 --> 01:06:57.791
[Vicenza chuckling] Hey!

1108
01:06:57.875 --> 01:06:59.250
[Paco] Hi!

1109
01:06:59.333 --> 01:07:00.791
Woo-hoo!

1110
01:07:14.625 --> 01:07:16.291
This party's the bomb, huh?

1111
01:07:16.375 --> 01:07:19.708
-[chuckling]
-The party is amazing! I'm loving it!

1112
01:07:53.208 --> 01:07:54.916
[laughing]

1113
01:07:56.333 --> 01:07:57.583
Hey!

1114
01:07:57.666 --> 01:08:00.208
Hey!

1115
01:08:00.291 --> 01:08:01.833
-What's up?
-Everything cool?

1116
01:08:01.916 --> 01:08:02.750
-Cool.
-Sweet.

1117
01:08:02.833 --> 01:08:05.041
-I'll have a drink, please, sir.
-What?

1118
01:08:05.125 --> 01:08:06.833
-It's for Betina! Thank you.
-[Paco] Huh?

1119
01:08:06.916 --> 01:08:07.750
It's for Betina.

1120
01:08:07.833 --> 01:08:08.708
I'm watching you!

1121
01:08:08.791 --> 01:08:10.833
-Okay, sounds good!
-You're on thin ice!

1122
01:08:15.916 --> 01:08:16.750
Arthur!

1123
01:08:17.625 --> 01:08:19.791
Huh? Paco!

1124
01:08:19.875 --> 01:08:21.375
Oh, you're such a pretty lady!

1125
01:08:21.458 --> 01:08:23.125
[both laughing]

1126
01:08:24.750 --> 01:08:26.583
What's up, what's up?

1127
01:08:26.666 --> 01:08:28.750
-Hey, Vicenza!
-Hey.

1128
01:08:28.833 --> 01:08:29.750
Bye, guys!

1129
01:08:29.833 --> 01:08:31.625
-[Giovanne] See ya.
-[blows kiss]

1130
01:08:31.708 --> 01:08:34.708
-What's up? Do you want a drink?
-Um, no, Vicenza,

1131
01:08:34.791 --> 01:08:37.750
it's just, um, I'm driving.
I shouldn't be drinking.

1132
01:08:38.333 --> 01:08:41.583
I think I'm gonna get water at the bar.
Yeah, I'll do that.

1133
01:08:50.000 --> 01:08:51.625
What's up? A sparkling water.

1134
01:08:51.708 --> 01:08:53.208
No, have a green juice.

1135
01:08:53.291 --> 01:08:55.416
[Giovanne] Green juice? Are you sure?

1136
01:08:55.500 --> 01:08:57.708
-[Paco] King Arthur!
-[both laughing]

1137
01:08:57.791 --> 01:08:59.291
I'm heading over there. See you.

1138
01:08:59.375 --> 01:09:00.708
[Arthur] Enjoy!

1139
01:09:00.791 --> 01:09:03.125
-I'll be right back, okay?
-Yeah? Okay.

1140
01:09:03.208 --> 01:09:04.583
[coughs]

1141
01:09:08.416 --> 01:09:09.833
Giovanne?

1142
01:09:09.916 --> 01:09:10.958
Arthur!

1143
01:09:11.041 --> 01:09:12.208
[both laughing]

1144
01:09:14.625 --> 01:09:16.416
My God! It's been too long a time!

1145
01:09:16.500 --> 01:09:18.375
-The Great Arthur!
-[chuckling]

1146
01:09:18.458 --> 01:09:19.458
Good to see you.

1147
01:09:19.541 --> 01:09:22.333
-So good to see you too, man.
-I'll be right back, okay?

1148
01:09:22.416 --> 01:09:24.500
-Go on, take care!
-Real quick. All right.

1149
01:09:24.583 --> 01:09:26.625
Hello? I need it now!

1150
01:09:27.291 --> 01:09:28.208
Hello?

1151
01:09:28.291 --> 01:09:31.250
-Hey, girl. Have you seen Paco?
-No, I haven't. Why?

1152
01:09:31.333 --> 01:09:32.791
Oh, my God.

1153
01:10:01.166 --> 01:10:03.625
Ugh, Cadu. I'm so tired of this.

1154
01:10:04.208 --> 01:10:07.208
Well, Vi, I mean,
why don't you  just come clean, then?

1155
01:10:07.291 --> 01:10:09.708
But I'm about to get
the test results, Cadu.

1156
01:10:09.791 --> 01:10:10.625
Vicenza?

1157
01:10:11.416 --> 01:10:13.375
Vicenza. I'm going home, okay?

1158
01:10:14.250 --> 01:10:15.666
-[kisses]
-Okay.

1159
01:10:15.750 --> 01:10:16.625
Congratulations.

1160
01:10:16.708 --> 01:10:18.166
-Aww.
-The party was great.

1161
01:10:18.250 --> 01:10:19.333
Thank you.

1162
01:10:19.416 --> 01:10:21.541
Yeah, it really was. Super great.

1163
01:10:24.750 --> 01:10:27.083
-Get inside, it's getting cold.
-But it's hot.

1164
01:10:27.166 --> 01:10:29.958
No, it's cold. You better get inside.

1165
01:10:30.041 --> 01:10:33.541
You gotta cover your shoulders
and protect your neck from the cold too.

1166
01:10:33.625 --> 01:10:34.625
-Okay?
-Sure.

1167
01:10:34.708 --> 01:10:36.416
[Paco] Okay, that's it, then.

1168
01:10:36.500 --> 01:10:38.666
-You should avoid the drizzle, okay?
-Sure.

1169
01:10:38.750 --> 01:10:42.708
You're saying sure, but you're not moving.
You gotta say "sure" then get inside!

1170
01:10:42.791 --> 01:10:45.958
It's like a wind tunnel out there,
so, I dunno, you'll get sick!

1171
01:10:46.041 --> 01:10:48.166
Like, three or four days in bed!

1172
01:10:48.791 --> 01:10:50.583
-Bye, Paco!
-See you, Paco!

1173
01:10:50.666 --> 01:10:51.666
[Paco] Bye!

1174
01:10:51.750 --> 01:10:53.750
[both chuckling]

1175
01:10:57.875 --> 01:10:59.000
Vicenza.

1176
01:11:00.708 --> 01:11:01.916
I'm gonna go.

1177
01:11:02.000 --> 01:11:03.916
-I have to wake up for work soon.
-Mm-hmm.

1178
01:11:04.000 --> 01:11:05.958
-I loved it.
-[Vicenza] Aw.

1179
01:11:06.666 --> 01:11:07.500
[kisses]

1180
01:11:08.833 --> 01:11:10.416
-Bye.
-Bye.

1181
01:11:11.791 --> 01:11:12.833
[Vicenza sighs]

1182
01:11:12.916 --> 01:11:15.250
Oh, Cadu! It all worked out!

1183
01:11:19.333 --> 01:11:20.583
I've never been kissed.

1184
01:11:22.291 --> 01:11:25.083
And I've never kissed someone
I had such strong feelings for.

1185
01:11:25.750 --> 01:11:29.708
And so… maybe our first kiss
should happen somewhere special.

1186
01:11:29.791 --> 01:11:30.875
Sure.

1187
01:11:31.458 --> 01:11:34.375
-Can Betina lend us her car?
-She already did.

1188
01:11:34.458 --> 01:11:36.083
-Shall we?
-Let's go.

1189
01:11:36.166 --> 01:11:37.208
[both chuckle]

1190
01:11:45.750 --> 01:11:47.791
-[horn honking]
-[exclaiming]

1191
01:11:48.541 --> 01:11:49.500
What the hell, man?

1192
01:11:49.583 --> 01:11:51.416
[thumping] Whoa, whoa, whoa!

1193
01:11:51.500 --> 01:11:53.250
Hey, man! What? Didn't you see me?

1194
01:11:53.333 --> 01:11:54.375
Are you insane?

1195
01:11:54.458 --> 01:11:57.000
Shit, you're the insane one!
Nearly ran me over!

1196
01:11:57.083 --> 01:11:58.208
Paco?

1197
01:11:59.416 --> 01:12:00.250
Giovanne?

1198
01:12:00.333 --> 01:12:01.583
[laughing]

1199
01:12:01.666 --> 01:12:04.333
Damn, it's been too long, bro!

1200
01:12:04.416 --> 01:12:06.500
Way too long, man!

1201
01:12:06.583 --> 01:12:08.416
Dude! You're doing well?

1202
01:12:08.500 --> 01:12:11.333
Yeah. You know, close call, but yeah.

1203
01:12:11.416 --> 01:12:12.666
[both chuckling]

1204
01:12:12.750 --> 01:12:14.208
That's a big gulp.

1205
01:12:14.291 --> 01:12:16.333
Get in the car. I'll drive you home.

1206
01:12:16.416 --> 01:12:18.500
I'll get inside, but we're not going home.

1207
01:12:18.583 --> 01:12:20.708
It's our little after-party!
Just a tiny one.

1208
01:12:20.791 --> 01:12:23.125
[Giovanne] Oh, boy. You got energy, huh?

1209
01:12:23.208 --> 01:12:24.333
[Paco] Nice car.

1210
01:12:24.416 --> 01:12:25.708
[laughing]

1211
01:12:28.041 --> 01:12:31.791
-[Paco] Yo, thanks for not taking me home.
-[Giovanne laughing]

1212
01:12:31.875 --> 01:12:34.166
Wanna go for a swim?
Still afraid of cold water?

1213
01:12:34.250 --> 01:12:36.208
[Giovanne]
I'm not afraid. Are you insane?

1214
01:12:36.291 --> 01:12:37.500
I'm terrified of it!

1215
01:12:37.583 --> 01:12:38.583
[both laughing]

1216
01:12:38.666 --> 01:12:40.666
-I'm so happy I ran into you.
-Me too.

1217
01:12:40.750 --> 01:12:41.875
Let's go for a swim.

1218
01:12:42.416 --> 01:12:43.666
[stomach gurgling]

1219
01:12:43.750 --> 01:12:44.625
What's wrong?

1220
01:12:44.708 --> 01:12:47.958
No, it's just the green juice
I had at the party.

1221
01:12:48.041 --> 01:12:50.500
I've got a great story to tell.
You won't believe it.

1222
01:12:50.583 --> 01:12:51.916
Yeah, tell me, tell me.

1223
01:12:52.000 --> 01:12:53.375
I'll tell you in a minute.

1224
01:12:53.458 --> 01:12:54.750
[gagging]

1225
01:12:58.875 --> 01:13:00.416
[both chuckling]

1226
01:13:03.416 --> 01:13:05.666
-This place is gorgeous, huh?
-Yeah, gorgeous.

1227
01:13:06.166 --> 01:13:08.333
Know what else is gorgeous? You.

1228
01:13:13.000 --> 01:13:14.916
[yelling] Oh, hey!

1229
01:13:15.750 --> 01:13:19.000
Get your hands off my daughter!
Get your hands off  my daughter!

1230
01:13:19.083 --> 01:13:21.375
Daughter? What daughter?
She's my daughter!

1231
01:13:21.458 --> 01:13:23.666
-Quit it, kid.
-What do you mean?

1232
01:13:23.750 --> 01:13:25.625
Your daughter? What's this, Vicenza?

1233
01:13:25.708 --> 01:13:28.291
-Calm down! I can explain!
-Hold on. How did you two meet?

1234
01:13:28.375 --> 01:13:29.958
-Shh!
-Shut up!

1235
01:13:30.041 --> 01:13:31.125
Okay.

1236
01:13:31.208 --> 01:13:33.791
Uh, I never knew who my father was,

1237
01:13:33.875 --> 01:13:35.875
then suddenly
I found myself with two dads.

1238
01:13:35.958 --> 01:13:38.083
-Two dads?
-What are you saying?

1239
01:13:38.166 --> 01:13:41.583
In the Naked Amoeba's archive,
I found photos of you two with Mom.

1240
01:13:41.666 --> 01:13:43.375
You just went looking for Giovanne?

1241
01:13:43.458 --> 01:13:46.375
-He could be my dad too!
-Why didn't you tell me about Paco?

1242
01:13:46.458 --> 01:13:49.375
-I didn't want to hurt you, so I--
-Hurt us? [laughing]

1243
01:13:49.458 --> 01:13:52.125
Hurt us? Give me a break, Vicenza.

1244
01:13:52.208 --> 01:13:53.666
-You were misleading us?
-She was.

1245
01:13:53.750 --> 01:13:55.625
-No!
-For the love of God, she was trying--

1246
01:13:55.708 --> 01:13:57.541
-[groaning] Shh!
-Shut up!

1247
01:14:02.625 --> 01:14:04.000
Look, if you ask me…

1248
01:14:05.208 --> 01:14:06.791
I think she's your daughter, Paco.

1249
01:14:08.166 --> 01:14:09.583
She's as selfish as you are.

1250
01:14:10.416 --> 01:14:12.125
Well, I think she's your daughter.

1251
01:14:14.291 --> 01:14:15.958
Insensitive.

1252
01:14:16.041 --> 01:14:17.291
Manipulative.

1253
01:14:19.541 --> 01:14:21.083
I introduced your mother to him!

1254
01:14:21.166 --> 01:14:22.958
-You never hooked up!
-You know nothing!

1255
01:14:23.041 --> 01:14:25.000
-Stop it! Both of you!
-[Paco] Shut up!

1256
01:14:31.750 --> 01:14:32.583
[sighs]

1257
01:14:33.166 --> 01:14:34.916
-So you're leaving, Paco?
-[Paco] Yeah.

1258
01:14:35.000 --> 01:14:37.500
-[Giovanne] You never grew up, did you?
-No, I didn't.

1259
01:14:47.875 --> 01:14:48.750
[Cadu] Don't worry.

1260
01:14:48.833 --> 01:14:50.000
-Cadu.
-Calm down.

1261
01:14:51.000 --> 01:14:52.750
[sobbing] I love them so much!

1262
01:14:53.583 --> 01:14:56.291
[sniffles] And now I've lost both of them.

1263
01:14:56.375 --> 01:14:58.208
You didn't. They love you very much.

1264
01:14:59.541 --> 01:15:02.333
But come on, I told you
this was not going to end well.

1265
01:15:03.750 --> 01:15:05.541
-Cadu, please leave.
-No. What--

1266
01:15:05.625 --> 01:15:07.916
I gotta be alone for a minute.
Go away, please.

1267
01:15:08.000 --> 01:15:08.833
Vicenza.

1268
01:15:56.666 --> 01:15:57.708
[phone ringing]

1269
01:16:20.208 --> 01:16:21.166
Ju!

1270
01:16:22.541 --> 01:16:23.375
Yes?

1271
01:16:23.458 --> 01:16:24.541
I'm going home.

1272
01:16:36.083 --> 01:16:36.916
Vicenza?

1273
01:16:38.375 --> 01:16:41.625
Vicenza, where were you?
Why haven't you picked up my calls?

1274
01:16:41.708 --> 01:16:42.666
I don't wanna talk.

1275
01:16:42.750 --> 01:16:45.125
Come on, I was worried,
and this is how you treat me?

1276
01:16:45.208 --> 01:16:47.291
You think I owe you anything, Cadu?

1277
01:16:47.791 --> 01:16:49.041
Yeah, I think you do.

1278
01:16:51.500 --> 01:16:54.291
Do you have any idea
how my mind is right now?

1279
01:16:54.375 --> 01:16:57.458
Do you know how it feels
to go from never having a father,

1280
01:16:58.041 --> 01:16:59.041
to finding one,

1281
01:16:59.541 --> 01:17:01.000
then finding another one,

1282
01:17:01.083 --> 01:17:03.750
then managing to lose
both of them right after that?

1283
01:17:03.833 --> 01:17:06.333
And all that's my fault.
Do you know?

1284
01:17:07.958 --> 01:17:09.208
No, you don't.

1285
01:17:09.958 --> 01:17:11.166
-Vicenza.
-Cadu.

1286
01:17:13.458 --> 01:17:14.458
Don't go there.

1287
01:17:16.166 --> 01:17:17.541
Just give her some time.

1288
01:17:18.583 --> 01:17:21.375
-She needs to be alone for a while.
-[door opens and closes]

1289
01:17:21.458 --> 01:17:24.041
Tomorrow, you two can talk then. Mm? 

1290
01:17:27.583 --> 01:17:29.291
[keypad clicking]

1291
01:17:42.708 --> 01:17:44.458
[phones pinging]

1292
01:17:53.958 --> 01:17:56.416
♪ If I have to
I will take a boat ♪

1293
01:17:56.500 --> 01:18:00.833
♪ I will row for six months like a fish
Just to see you ♪

1294
01:18:01.750 --> 01:18:04.666
♪ There's no sea large enough ♪

1295
01:18:04.750 --> 01:18:08.208
♪ To scare me
To make me give up on you ♪

1296
01:18:09.208 --> 01:18:12.500
♪ If I have to
I will build a machine ♪

1297
01:18:12.583 --> 01:18:16.583
♪ Faster than doubt
More sudden than a tear ♪

1298
01:18:16.666 --> 01:18:21.041
♪ I will travel at full power
And in a moment of pain from missing you ♪

1299
01:18:21.125 --> 01:18:24.625
♪ I will be there to tell you
That I came to see you ♪

1300
01:18:25.041 --> 01:18:27.000
♪ I want to share ♪

1301
01:18:27.083 --> 01:18:31.541
♪ I want to share the good life with you ♪

1302
01:18:32.708 --> 01:18:34.833
♪ I want to share ♪

1303
01:18:34.916 --> 01:18:41.583
♪ I want to share the good life with you ♪

1304
01:18:43.708 --> 01:18:44.583
Vicenza, I…

1305
01:18:46.250 --> 01:18:47.666
What's going on Vicenza?

1306
01:18:47.750 --> 01:18:49.000
Where are you going?

1307
01:18:49.083 --> 01:18:51.833
-I'm going home. I don't belong here.
-Huh?

1308
01:18:51.916 --> 01:18:55.291
My mother was right, Cadu.
I wasn't supposed to meet my dad.

1309
01:18:56.250 --> 01:18:57.250
Are you sure?

1310
01:18:58.291 --> 01:18:59.875
Are those the results?

1311
01:19:00.916 --> 01:19:01.750
Vicenza…

1312
01:19:03.000 --> 01:19:03.875
I'm sorry.

1313
01:19:03.958 --> 01:19:06.625
There's something going on downstairs.
You have visitors.

1314
01:19:06.708 --> 01:19:08.083
What's up, Cadu? See ya.

1315
01:19:16.291 --> 01:19:17.333
Mom?

1316
01:19:18.541 --> 01:19:21.166
[Raion] Oh, my love!

1317
01:19:22.166 --> 01:19:24.333
Oh, I missed you so much. Are you okay?

1318
01:19:24.416 --> 01:19:25.916
Mm-hmm, I'm okay.

1319
01:19:26.000 --> 01:19:27.750
[snapping fingers]

1320
01:19:27.833 --> 01:19:29.333
Mother Moon!

1321
01:19:29.416 --> 01:19:31.708
[chuckling]

1322
01:19:33.708 --> 01:19:35.291
Hi, everyone!

1323
01:19:41.625 --> 01:19:44.416
-Mom, how did you find me here?
-I'm a mother, aren't I?

1324
01:19:44.500 --> 01:19:47.416
I got home, then I noticed
you discovered Paco's picture,

1325
01:19:47.500 --> 01:19:50.208
so I put two and two together,
and came here to look for him.

1326
01:19:50.291 --> 01:19:52.916
Exactly. That's where I come in.
I was walking outside.

1327
01:19:53.000 --> 01:19:56.041
I even mistook her for you.
Then it hit me, it all made sense.

1328
01:19:56.125 --> 01:19:58.666
Everyone's wearing costumes.
That's Vicenza's troupe!

1329
01:19:58.750 --> 01:20:01.083
[all laughing]

1330
01:20:01.166 --> 01:20:04.083
That's exactly how it was.
But our cute moment is over now.

1331
01:20:04.166 --> 01:20:07.541
Vicenza, how dare you run away?
You're absolutely insane!

1332
01:20:08.208 --> 01:20:10.333
I'm sorry.
I know I shouldn't have run away.

1333
01:20:11.791 --> 01:20:16.916
Owning up to your mistakes
is a beautiful sign of maturity, sweetie.

1334
01:20:17.500 --> 01:20:19.375
And Mommy has made mistakes too.

1335
01:20:19.458 --> 01:20:23.791
In India, Mommy realized
that she's not that esoteric after all.

1336
01:20:23.875 --> 01:20:29.000
And that, even though I'm your mom,
I just can't control your life

1337
01:20:29.083 --> 01:20:31.750
the way I would like to control it,
unfortunately.

1338
01:20:31.833 --> 01:20:34.041
I learned that from the flies.

1339
01:20:34.125 --> 01:20:35.083
What flies?

1340
01:20:35.666 --> 01:20:38.458
My cutie-pie, there were so many flies.
Everywhere.

1341
01:20:38.541 --> 01:20:41.708
And you couldn't even scare them off.

1342
01:20:41.791 --> 01:20:43.750
And then, what did Mommy figure out?

1343
01:20:43.833 --> 01:20:48.416
That you can try to control yourself.
But other people? That's impossible.

1344
01:20:48.500 --> 01:20:52.583
If someone wants to kill a bunch of flies,
all we can do is to understand.

1345
01:20:52.666 --> 01:20:54.708
I'll be forever grateful to the flies

1346
01:20:54.791 --> 01:20:59.208
for being able to show me that,
contrary to what I've always said,

1347
01:20:59.958 --> 01:21:02.375
you have every right
to know who your father is.

1348
01:21:11.250 --> 01:21:12.375
What is that?

1349
01:21:12.958 --> 01:21:15.458
It's the DNA test I did
with Paco and Giovanne.

1350
01:21:17.458 --> 01:21:18.916
Giovanne as well?

1351
01:21:19.500 --> 01:21:21.333
Yeah, I found him too.

1352
01:21:22.041 --> 01:21:23.416
Oh, my love…

1353
01:21:23.500 --> 01:21:24.333
[kisses]

1354
01:21:25.416 --> 01:21:26.791
[Betina] Guys! Guys! Guys!

1355
01:21:26.875 --> 01:21:28.375
We're really screwed!

1356
01:21:28.458 --> 01:21:30.333
-What?
-The stage bus caught on fire!

1357
01:21:30.416 --> 01:21:31.541
Did anyone get hurt?

1358
01:21:31.625 --> 01:21:34.375
No, no one got hurt.
But everything was on it.

1359
01:21:34.458 --> 01:21:36.916
-Including the money.
-But how did that happen?

1360
01:21:37.000 --> 01:21:40.541
Um, it seems the stage bus I rented
couldn't handle that many lights.

1361
01:21:40.625 --> 01:21:42.041
Dang it, Betina.

1362
01:21:43.125 --> 01:21:45.458
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

1363
01:21:45.541 --> 01:21:48.583
Everything happens for a reason.
Doesn't it, Mother Moon?

1364
01:21:55.083 --> 01:21:56.208
-Mother Moon?
-Oh!

1365
01:21:56.291 --> 01:21:58.291
Of course, of course! Yeah!

1366
01:21:58.375 --> 01:21:59.583
Uh, I agree with you.

1367
01:21:59.666 --> 01:22:00.666
[Raion] Right?

1368
01:22:00.750 --> 01:22:02.625
[Mother Moon]
We've gotta change the energy.

1369
01:22:02.708 --> 01:22:04.458
So come on, everyone.

1370
01:22:04.541 --> 01:22:08.250
[all inhale and exhale deeply]

1371
01:22:11.625 --> 01:22:13.333
[snapping fingers rhythmically]

1372
01:22:24.291 --> 01:22:25.291
I got it, guys!

1373
01:22:27.000 --> 01:22:28.875
The fire was a sign.

1374
01:22:30.958 --> 01:22:33.708
I'm sorry, Betina,
but this fire was a sign

1375
01:22:33.791 --> 01:22:36.958
that the Naked Amoeba
should parade like in the good old days.

1376
01:22:37.041 --> 01:22:38.541
With samba, Carnival songs.

1377
01:22:39.125 --> 01:22:42.333
With instruments and singing,
and nothing else.

1378
01:22:42.416 --> 01:22:46.250
Yeah, that sounds like the Amoeba.
Good old-fashioned Carnival.

1379
01:22:46.333 --> 01:22:49.208
I don't know what I was thinking,
trying something new.

1380
01:22:49.291 --> 01:22:50.666
[Arthur] Oh, my sweet girl.

1381
01:22:50.750 --> 01:22:52.291
Look, listen up, I, uh…

1382
01:22:52.375 --> 01:22:55.375
I know everyone's a bit shaken
with all that just happened,

1383
01:22:55.458 --> 01:22:56.916
but Vicenza is right.

1384
01:22:57.000 --> 01:23:01.000
You know? Yeah. 'Cause we gotta do it
like the good old days, man!

1385
01:23:01.083 --> 01:23:02.625
-[laughing]
-[Arthur] Yeah!

1386
01:23:02.708 --> 01:23:03.666
So, you…

1387
01:23:04.375 --> 01:23:07.625
I want you to get every student
who can play percussion.

1388
01:23:07.708 --> 01:23:09.500
I got it. The teachers too, right?

1389
01:23:09.583 --> 01:23:11.458
You should get everyone. Yeah.

1390
01:23:11.541 --> 01:23:14.666
Because we're going to party
and parade in the streets.

1391
01:23:14.750 --> 01:23:15.791
It'll be amazing!

1392
01:23:15.875 --> 01:23:17.458
[all chattering in excitement]

1393
01:23:17.541 --> 01:23:19.083
Rejoice, my good people!

1394
01:23:19.166 --> 01:23:21.583
Hooray for the Naked Amoeba!

1395
01:23:21.666 --> 01:23:22.625
[all] Hooray!

1396
01:23:22.708 --> 01:23:24.166
[all cheering]

1397
01:23:24.250 --> 01:23:25.875
It's going to be beautiful!

1398
01:23:25.958 --> 01:23:28.291
-[Arthur] Yeah, it will be.
-Like you.

1399
01:23:29.708 --> 01:23:30.666
[chuckling]

1400
01:23:30.750 --> 01:23:32.208
[Mother Moon] Nice to meet you.

1401
01:23:32.291 --> 01:23:33.875
My pleasure. I'm Arthur. Thank you.

1402
01:23:33.958 --> 01:23:35.125
Mother Moon.

1403
01:23:35.208 --> 01:23:36.208
[kisses]

1404
01:23:36.291 --> 01:23:37.208
Mother Moon.

1405
01:23:39.458 --> 01:23:40.458
[kisses]

1406
01:23:40.541 --> 01:23:41.958
But you can call me…

1407
01:23:42.625 --> 01:23:43.458
Moon.

1408
01:23:43.541 --> 01:23:45.375
[both laughing]

1409
01:24:01.166 --> 01:24:02.791
[no audible dialogue]

1410
01:24:08.583 --> 01:24:11.250
When we get to New York,
there will be a press conference.

1411
01:24:11.333 --> 01:24:15.125
Then you'll have a newspaper interview.
It can be through e-mail or text.

1412
01:24:15.625 --> 01:24:17.125
That night isn't gonna work…

1413
01:24:17.208 --> 01:24:19.208
[continues inaudibly]

1414
01:24:25.083 --> 01:24:26.541
[doorbell chimes]

1415
01:24:29.416 --> 01:24:30.666
Let's go to Disney!

1416
01:24:30.750 --> 01:24:32.000
[low energy] Yay.

1417
01:24:32.750 --> 01:24:35.208
-[Marta] Good morning, Giovanne.
-Good morning.

1418
01:24:37.166 --> 01:24:39.250
Look after those kids, please, okay?

1419
01:24:39.333 --> 01:24:40.375
You got it.

1420
01:24:45.208 --> 01:24:46.125
[sarcastic] Yay!

1421
01:24:49.750 --> 01:24:52.625
Guys, guys, guys! Hear me out!

1422
01:24:52.708 --> 01:24:56.250
I just got off the phone
with Ivete Sangalo, and she confirmed

1423
01:24:56.333 --> 01:24:58.041
she is in fact not coming!

1424
01:24:58.125 --> 01:24:59.666
[all laugh]

1425
01:24:59.750 --> 01:25:02.666
But I'm here!
Let's party, people! Come on!

1426
01:25:09.666 --> 01:25:12.083
-My shoe came off!
-For the love of God, Guilherme!

1427
01:25:12.166 --> 01:25:13.625
Where did you drop it?

1428
01:25:14.208 --> 01:25:16.833
-Here, Betina.
-Oh, thanks.

1429
01:25:16.916 --> 01:25:19.791
I think there's something wrong
with the speaker. Can you check?

1430
01:25:19.875 --> 01:25:21.541
Of course. We'll fix it. Thanks.

1431
01:25:23.000 --> 01:25:24.791
Vicenza! Vicenza.

1432
01:25:24.875 --> 01:25:26.708
[gasps] No way!

1433
01:25:27.458 --> 01:25:29.625
What are you doing here?

1434
01:25:29.708 --> 01:25:31.833
I couldn't miss your first Carnival.

1435
01:25:31.916 --> 01:25:33.958
-What about the art show?
-I'll do it later.

1436
01:25:34.041 --> 01:25:38.041
Oh, that's wonderful! I thought
you'd never want to see me again.

1437
01:25:38.125 --> 01:25:40.208
Come on, that's how families are.

1438
01:25:40.291 --> 01:25:42.625
Families fight, argue,
but then we make up.

1439
01:25:42.708 --> 01:25:44.208
[both chuckle]

1440
01:25:45.833 --> 01:25:46.791
Vicenza!

1441
01:25:48.833 --> 01:25:50.833
Did you forgive me too?

1442
01:25:50.916 --> 01:25:51.833
Of course.

1443
01:25:51.916 --> 01:25:53.083
What about Disney?

1444
01:25:53.875 --> 01:25:55.708
Well, it looks like…

1445
01:25:56.416 --> 01:25:58.875
they hate Disney and love you.

1446
01:26:01.583 --> 01:26:03.916
I don't want to go anywhere
without you, Vicenza.

1447
01:26:06.791 --> 01:26:07.875
[Vicenza] Guys,

1448
01:26:07.958 --> 01:26:09.666
I-I really love you.

1449
01:26:10.375 --> 01:26:11.208
So much.

1450
01:26:11.875 --> 01:26:15.000
But I had to find out
which one of you is my real dad.

1451
01:26:16.041 --> 01:26:18.875
So, I took a DNA test and now I know.

1452
01:26:20.750 --> 01:26:22.750
Can you close your eyes really quick?

1453
01:26:25.000 --> 01:26:27.375
I just have to do something.
It's important.

1454
01:26:27.458 --> 01:26:28.416
All right.

1455
01:26:29.250 --> 01:26:30.083
Please?

1456
01:26:32.791 --> 01:26:35.916
Wow, my heart is…
It's almost jumping out of my throat.

1457
01:26:36.000 --> 01:26:37.250
Yeah, same for me.

1458
01:26:38.166 --> 01:26:39.000
Close your eyes.

1459
01:26:39.083 --> 01:26:41.541
You're trying to kill us
with the suspense, right?

1460
01:26:41.625 --> 01:26:43.750
Calm down, guys. You'll like it.

1461
01:26:45.416 --> 01:26:46.958
Paco, you can't peek.

1462
01:26:47.833 --> 01:26:49.041
[Paco] What is this?

1463
01:26:49.416 --> 01:26:51.166
Stay still. There.

1464
01:26:55.250 --> 01:26:57.500
So, when I say "go,"

1465
01:26:57.583 --> 01:26:59.791
both of you open your eyes
at the same time

1466
01:26:59.875 --> 01:27:01.875
and read the paper
on the other's forehead.

1467
01:27:01.958 --> 01:27:03.291
-Okay?
-Okay.

1468
01:27:04.583 --> 01:27:05.708
Three…

1469
01:27:06.708 --> 01:27:07.791
two…

1470
01:27:08.666 --> 01:27:10.708
one… go!

1471
01:27:12.583 --> 01:27:15.375
[both]
"Do you want to be Vicenza's father?"

1472
01:27:17.541 --> 01:27:19.791
-What? I don't get it.
-Yeah, me neither.

1473
01:27:21.375 --> 01:27:22.625
Neither of you are my dad.

1474
01:27:24.708 --> 01:27:26.083
I'm sorry, I don't follow.

1475
01:27:27.333 --> 01:27:29.416
Guys, I think that's good.

1476
01:27:30.916 --> 01:27:34.708
It means what I have with you two
is much stronger than any blood ties.

1477
01:27:36.125 --> 01:27:39.000
Because a real father
wants to be with his kid.

1478
01:27:40.125 --> 01:27:44.166
Look where you are,
on such an important day for you both.

1479
01:27:46.750 --> 01:27:48.333
What I want to have with you…

1480
01:27:48.458 --> 01:27:50.125
[sniffles]

1481
01:27:50.250 --> 01:27:51.250
It's real.

1482
01:27:53.458 --> 01:27:54.416
I love you, Dad.

1483
01:27:54.500 --> 01:27:56.125
[Paco chuckles]

1484
01:27:56.750 --> 01:27:57.708
I love you, Dad.

1485
01:28:00.083 --> 01:28:01.250
Do you want to be my dad?

1486
01:28:04.958 --> 01:28:06.458
Do you want to be my dad?

1487
01:28:09.250 --> 01:28:10.916
Do you accept being my dads?

1488
01:28:13.666 --> 01:28:15.208
I already feel like your dad.

1489
01:28:18.125 --> 01:28:19.250
It's an honor.

1490
01:28:25.125 --> 01:28:28.666
Aw, that's so cute,
the three of you together!

1491
01:28:28.750 --> 01:28:30.083
-Mom!
-[Paco] Wow.

1492
01:28:30.166 --> 01:28:31.541
[Raion chuckling]

1493
01:28:31.625 --> 01:28:33.541
-Raion!
-Hi, Paco.

1494
01:28:36.083 --> 01:28:39.000
-Hi, Giovanne.
-Hi, Raion. Weren't you in India?

1495
01:28:39.083 --> 01:28:39.916
Well, yeah.

1496
01:28:40.833 --> 01:28:44.041
But I had to come back
so I could talk to this piece of work.

1497
01:28:44.916 --> 01:28:45.750
My sweetie.

1498
01:28:46.750 --> 01:28:49.125
Here you go. Everything
you've always wanted to know.

1499
01:28:50.000 --> 01:28:53.208
Name, address
and phone number of your real father.

1500
01:28:55.625 --> 01:28:57.541
He never wanted to hear from you,

1501
01:28:58.333 --> 01:29:02.125
but I can't really keep you
from knowing him forever.

1502
01:29:46.541 --> 01:29:47.625
I already have a dad.

1503
01:29:50.208 --> 01:29:51.125
Two, actually.

1504
01:29:55.958 --> 01:29:57.625
Vi! Hi, everyone.

1505
01:29:57.708 --> 01:29:59.208
It's about to start. Coming?

1506
01:29:59.833 --> 01:30:00.833
Let's go.

1507
01:30:01.500 --> 01:30:02.375
Come on!

1508
01:30:05.500 --> 01:30:07.500
NAKED AMOEBA

1509
01:30:16.291 --> 01:30:18.750
[Original Carnival song playing]

1510
01:32:04.916 --> 01:32:06.500
[song ends]

1511
01:32:06.583 --> 01:32:08.500
[soft instrumental music plays]

1512
01:32:58.000 --> 01:32:59.833
[Mother Moon] We grow everything.

1513
01:33:00.875 --> 01:33:02.583
-Hey!
-[Raion] Hey, check it out.

1514
01:33:07.916 --> 01:33:08.750
It's lovely.

1515
01:33:11.500 --> 01:33:12.625
It's beautiful, honey.

1516
01:33:13.458 --> 01:33:14.875
You're really special.

1517
01:33:14.958 --> 01:33:18.625
Brigadeiro made of banana biomass
and 79% cocoa.

1518
01:33:18.708 --> 01:33:20.875
But I swear it's delicious. Paco?

1519
01:33:20.958 --> 01:33:22.000
No, thanks.

1520
01:33:23.375 --> 01:33:24.708
Wow, sweetie.

1521
01:33:24.791 --> 01:33:25.875
It's beautiful.

1522
01:33:26.458 --> 01:33:27.916
[Cadu] Paco, Giovanne.

1523
01:33:28.791 --> 01:33:30.333
-Psst!
-What are you doing?

1524
01:33:30.416 --> 01:33:33.500
You guys are unbelievable. Come on, Cadu.

1525
01:33:33.583 --> 01:33:35.291
-Where are you going?
-Yeah, where?

1526
01:33:35.375 --> 01:33:37.708
-'Cause if you need company, I'll go.
-Me too.

1527
01:33:37.791 --> 01:33:38.625
Yeah.

1528
01:33:38.708 --> 01:33:42.416
Vicenza Shakti Pravananda
Oxalá Sarahara Zalala…

1529
01:33:42.500 --> 01:33:44.250
da Silva Benizatto Costa.

1530
01:33:44.333 --> 01:33:46.125
-Respect your father.
-Fathers!

1531
01:33:46.208 --> 01:33:47.791
Fathers, yes. Your fathers.

1532
01:33:47.875 --> 01:33:51.000
On our trip to the ranch next week,
everyone will walk together.

1533
01:33:51.083 --> 01:33:53.416
-That's right.
-The kids, you two, Paco.

1534
01:33:53.500 --> 01:33:55.208
Like an excursion. My trip, my rules.

1535
01:33:55.291 --> 01:33:57.666
Oh, God. Go!

1536
01:33:57.750 --> 01:34:00.500
I'll take care of these two.
Let them make out.

1537
01:34:00.583 --> 01:34:03.333
-Make out? What does she mean?
-What do you mean by "make out"?

1538
01:34:03.416 --> 01:34:05.500
I don't think Vicenza
is old enough to make out.

1539
01:34:05.583 --> 01:34:08.125
-Of course not. You're right.
-Hey, I'm 18 years old!

1540
01:34:08.208 --> 01:34:09.458
[Paco] That's the point!

1541
01:34:09.541 --> 01:34:13.166
Listen, put on a coat
because it's getting colder.

1542
01:34:13.250 --> 01:34:14.833
A hoodie! A beanie too!

1543
01:34:14.916 --> 01:34:18.750
Yeah, and a, um…a scarf, a shawl,
something around your neck!

1544
01:34:18.833 --> 01:34:20.125
Around the neck, yeah.

1545
01:34:20.208 --> 01:34:22.208
-This Cadu, huh?
-[chuckling]

1546
01:34:22.291 --> 01:34:23.791
He is clearly a psychopath.

1547
01:34:23.875 --> 01:34:25.750
-Oh, come on.
-Yeah.

1548
01:34:25.833 --> 01:34:27.083
He doesn't cut his nails.

1549
01:34:27.166 --> 01:34:30.083
But he doesn't cut his nails
because he plays guitar.

1550
01:34:30.166 --> 01:34:33.541
You're both ridiculous, guys!
Let the girl enjoy her life!

1551
01:34:33.625 --> 01:34:35.791
Look at this, what a beautiful painting.

1552
01:34:36.375 --> 01:34:38.208
You have the best daughter in the world.

1553
01:34:40.583 --> 01:34:42.666
-He's got hairy legs, though.
-Oh, no.

1554
01:34:42.750 --> 01:34:44.541
A grown man. He's not right for her.

1555
01:34:44.625 --> 01:34:47.291
Musician. He's really not right for her.
He's an artist.

1556
01:34:47.375 --> 01:34:49.625
What's wrong with that? I'm an artist too.

1557
01:34:49.708 --> 01:34:51.000
-So?
-That's the point.

1558
01:34:51.083 --> 01:34:52.500
-What's your point?
-Nothing.

1559
01:34:52.583 --> 01:34:53.458
[laughing]

1560
01:34:53.541 --> 01:34:54.875
-Oh, you guys…
-It's karma.

1561
01:34:54.958 --> 01:34:56.041
Huh?

1562
01:34:56.125 --> 01:34:58.208
-What do you mean? Fate?
-[chuckling] Please!

1563
01:35:00.958 --> 01:35:04.916
["Casa" by Nina Fernandes playing]

1564
01:38:58.125 --> 01:38:59.625
[song ends]

1565
01:39:01.166 --> 01:39:03.166
[cheerful instrumental music plays]
